window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-16-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 16 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Replace the question mark (?) in the series given below with suitable options.<br><br>4,10,25,62.5,156.25,? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे दी गई श्रृंखला में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर उपयुक्त विकल्प रखिए।<br><br>4,10,25,62.5,156.25,? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"145.25"},"2":{"en":"72.25"},"3":{"en":"390.625"},"4":{"en":"290"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each term is 2.5 times the term before it:<br>4 × 2.5 = 10, 10 × 2.5 = 25, 25 × 2.5 = 62.5, 62.5 × 2.5 = 156.25<br>Next = 156.25 × 2.5 = 390.625<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 390.625.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पूर्व पद का 2.5 गुना है:<br>4 × 2.5 = 10, 10 × 2.5 = 25, 25 × 2.5 = 62.5, 62.5 × 2.5 = 156.25<br>अगला = 156.25 × 2.5 = 390.625<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 390.625 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the option that has the same relationship with the third term as the second term has with the first.<br><br>BE:G ::IL:? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जिसका तीसरे पद के साथ वही संबंध है जो दूसरे पद का पहले पद के साथ है।<br><br>BE:G ::IL:? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"T"},"2":{"en":"R"},"3":{"en":"U"},"4":{"en":"S"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"B (2) + E (5) = 7 = G<br>So the third letter is the sum of the first two.<br>I (9) + L (12) = 21 = U<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): U.</b>","hi":"B (2) + E (5) = 7 = G<br>अर्थात् तीसरा अक्षर पहले दो अक्षरों का योग है।<br>I (9) + L (12) = 21 = U<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): U है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Each question has four options. Three of them go together based on a common idea or rule. One is different. Identify the one that is different. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रत्येक प्रश्न में चार विकल्प हैं। उनमें से तीन किसी सामान्य विचार या नियम के आधार पर एक साथ जाते हैं। एक भिन्न है। भिन्न वाले को पहचानें। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23 – 29"},"2":{"en":"19 – 25"},"3":{"en":"13 – 17"},"4":{"en":"3 – 5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"23, 29, 13, 17, 3 and 5 are all prime numbers.<br>In 19 – 25, the number 25 is not prime, so this pair is different.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 19 – 25.</b>","hi":"23, 29, 13, 17, 3 और 5 सभी अभाज्य संख्याएँ हैं।<br>19 – 25 में संख्या 25 अभाज्य नहीं है, इसलिए यह युग्म भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 19 – 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"In the sequence 'VGQCRKMWON', identify the letter at the 9<sup>th</sup> position after extracting letters from indices 3, 7, 8. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अनुक्रम 'VGQCRKMWON' में सूचकांक 3, 7, 8 के अक्षर निकालने के बाद 9<sup>वें</sup> स्थान का अक्षर पहचानें। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M"},"2":{"en":"O"},"3":{"en":"N"},"4":{"en":"Z"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Numbering from the left: V-1, G-2, Q-3, C-4, R-5, K-6, M-7, W-8, O-9, N-10.<br>The letters at indices 3, 7 and 8 are Q, M and W.<br>The letter at the 9th position is O.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): O.</b>","hi":"बाएँ से गिनने पर: V-1, G-2, Q-3, C-4, R-5, K-6, M-7, W-8, O-9, N-10।<br>सूचकांक 3, 7 और 8 के अक्षर Q, M और W हैं।<br>9<sup>वें</sup> स्थान का अक्षर O है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): O है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Problem Statement: A software company's customer support manager notices that response times are increasing as customer volume grows. The team can either hire more support staff (increasing costs) or implement automated chatbots (potentially reducing service quality). Customer satisfaction surveys show mixed reactions to automation.<br>How should the manager approach this capacity decision? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"समस्या कथन: एक सॉफ़्टवेयर कंपनी का ग्राहक सहायता प्रबंधक देखता है कि ग्राहक संख्या बढ़ने के साथ प्रतिक्रिया समय बढ़ रहा है। टीम या तो अधिक सहायता कर्मचारी नियुक्त कर सकती है (लागत बढ़ेगी) या स्वचालित चैटबॉट लागू कर सकती है (सेवा गुणवत्ता घट सकती है)। ग्राहक संतुष्टि सर्वेक्षण स्वचालन पर मिली-जुली प्रतिक्रियाएँ दिखाते हैं।<br>प्रबंधक को इस क्षमता निर्णय को कैसे लेना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hire more staff to maintain personal service quality","hi":"व्यक्तिगत सेवा गुणवत्ता बनाए रखने के लिए अधिक कर्मचारी नियुक्त करें"},"2":{"en":"Implement chatbots to manage costs and scale efficiently","hi":"लागत संभालने और कुशलता से विस्तार के लिए चैटबॉट लागू करें"},"3":{"en":"Analyze customer inquiry types to determine optimal mix of automated and human support","hi":"स्वचालित और मानव सहायता का सर्वोत्तम मिश्रण तय करने के लिए ग्राहक पूछताछ के प्रकारों का विश्लेषण करें"},"4":{"en":"Increase response time targets to manage expectations","hi":"अपेक्षाएँ संभालने के लिए प्रतिक्रिया समय लक्ष्य बढ़ा दें"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Both choices have a cost, so the manager must first find which types of queries suit automation and which need a human.<br>Option (3) does this study before deciding; the others pick one extreme or lower the service standard.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Analyze customer inquiry types to determine optimal mix of automated and human support.</b>","hi":"दोनों विकल्पों की अपनी लागत है, इसलिए प्रबंधक को पहले यह देखना चाहिए कि किस प्रकार की पूछताछ स्वचालन से हो सकती है और किसके लिए मानव चाहिए।<br>विकल्प (3) निर्णय से पहले यह अध्ययन करता है; शेष विकल्प एक अति चुनते हैं या सेवा मानक घटा देते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): स्वचालित और मानव सहायता का सर्वोत्तम मिश्रण तय करने के लिए ग्राहक पूछताछ के प्रकारों का विश्लेषण करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, if ECONOMIC = 56 and EFFICIENCY = 90, then what is the value of MANAGEMENT? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में यदि ECONOMIC = 56 और EFFICIENCY = 90 है, तो MANAGEMENT का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"120"},"3":{"en":"90"},"4":{"en":"80"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"ECONOMIC has 8 letters and 8 × 7 = 56<br>EFFICIENCY has 10 letters and 10 × 9 = 90<br>So the code = (number of letters) × (number of letters − 1)<br>MANAGEMENT has 10 letters → 10 × 9 = 90<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 90.</b>","hi":"ECONOMIC में 8 अक्षर हैं और 8 × 7 = 56<br>EFFICIENCY में 10 अक्षर हैं और 10 × 9 = 90<br>अतः कूट = (अक्षरों की संख्या) × (अक्षरों की संख्या − 1)<br>MANAGEMENT में 10 अक्षर हैं → 10 × 9 = 90<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 90 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Assuming that the data given in the statement are definitely true which of the following conclusions can be logically deducted from given statements.<br>Statement: “Smoking is prohibited in public areas.” – A law.<br>Conclusions:<br>I. Authorities are concerned about public health.<br>II. People have completely stopped smoking. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यह मानते हुए कि कथन में दिया गया डेटा निश्चित रूप से सत्य है, निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकाला जा सकता है।<br>कथन: \"सार्वजनिक स्थानों पर धूम्रपान निषिद्ध है।\" – एक कानून।<br>निष्कर्ष:<br>I. अधिकारी जनस्वास्थ्य के बारे में चिंतित हैं।<br>II. लोगों ने धूम्रपान पूरी तरह छोड़ दिया है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A ban on smoking in public places is made to protect people’s health, so the authorities are concerned about public health. I follows.<br>The law does not say that people have stopped smoking. II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"सार्वजनिक स्थानों पर धूम्रपान पर प्रतिबंध लागू लोगों के स्वास्थ्य की रक्षा के लिए होता है, इसलिए अधिकारी जनस्वास्थ्य के बारे में चिंतित हैं। I निकलता है।<br>कानून यह नहीं कहता कि लोगों ने धूम्रपान छोड़ दिया है। II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Some social issues, problem and their solution is provided to you as a statement you have to mark the logical action that can be taken under these conditions.<br>When communicating with someone from a different generation, the most effective approach is to: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कुछ सामाजिक मुद्दे, समस्या और उनका समाधान आपको कथन के रूप में दिए गए हैं, आपको वह तार्किक कार्रवाई चिह्नित करनी है जो इन परिस्थितियों में की जा सकती है।<br>भिन्न पीढ़ी के किसी व्यक्ति से संवाद करते समय सबसे प्रभावी तरीका है: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Use only your preferred communication style","hi":"केवल अपनी पसंदीदा संवाद शैली का प्रयोग करें"},"2":{"en":"Adapt your communication style to bridge generational differences","hi":"पीढ़ीगत अंतरों को पाटने के लिए अपनी संवाद शैली को अनुकूलित करें"},"3":{"en":"Avoid communication to prevent misunderstandings","hi":"गलतफ़हमियों से बचने के लिए संवाद से बचें"},"4":{"en":"Speak louder and slower","hi":"अधिक ज़ोर से और धीरे बोलें"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Communication succeeds when the speaker adjusts to the listener, and here the gap is of generation.<br>Option (2) builds that bridge; using only one style, avoiding talk or just speaking louder does not solve the difference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Adapt your communication style to bridge generational differences.</b>","hi":"संवाद तब सफल होता है जब वक्ता श्रोता के अनुसार ढलता है, और यहाँ अंतर पीढ़ी का है।<br>विकल्प (2) यही सेतु बनाता है; केवल एक शैली अपनाना, बातचीत से बचना या ज़ोर से बोलना अंतर नहीं मिटाते।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): पीढ़ीगत अंतरों को पाटने के लिए अपनी संवाद शैली को अनुकूलित करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What should come at the place of question mark? : 3, 4, 6, 9, 13, 18, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर क्या आना चाहिए? : 3, 4, 6, 9, 13, 18, ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24"},"2":{"en":"25"},"3":{"en":"26"},"4":{"en":"27"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Differences: +1, +2, +3, +4, +5<br>Next difference = +6 → 18 + 6 = 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 24.</b>","hi":"अंतर: +1, +2, +3, +4, +5<br>अगला अंतर = +6 → 18 + 6 = 24<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"some of the equations are provided below with symbols and mathematical relations you have to check which of the following combination is correct<br>If A ‡ B = (A<sup>2</sup> + B) × B, find 3 ‡ 2. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे कुछ समीकरण चिह्नों और गणितीय संबंधों के साथ दिए गए हैं, आपको जाँचना है कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा संयोजन सही है<br>यदि A ‡ B = (A<sup>2</sup> + B) × B है, तो 3 ‡ 2 ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"22"},"4":{"en":"16"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A ‡ B = (A<sup>2</sup> + B) × B<br>3 ‡ 2 = (3<sup>2</sup> + 2) × 2 = (9 + 2) × 2 = 11 × 2 = 22<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 22.</b>","hi":"A ‡ B = (A<sup>2</sup> + B) × B<br>3 ‡ 2 = (3<sup>2</sup> + 2) × 2 = (9 + 2) × 2 = 11 × 2 = 22<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 22 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Directions: From the given alternative words, select the word which can not be formed using the letters of the given word.ABSOLUTELY. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: दिए गए वैकल्पिक शब्दों में से वह शब्द चुनिए जो दिए गए शब्द ABSOLUTELY के अक्षरों से नहीं बनाया जा सकता। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ABSOLUTE"},"2":{"en":"BALLUTES"},"3":{"en":"OBLATELY"},"4":{"en":"OBLAATELY"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"ABSOLUTELY has A-1, B-1, S-1, O-1, L-2, U-1, T-1, E-1, Y-1.<br>OBLAATELY needs the letter A twice, but the given word has only one A, so it cannot be formed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): OBLAATELY.</b>","hi":"ABSOLUTELY में A-1, B-1, S-1, O-1, L-2, U-1, T-1, E-1, Y-1 हैं।<br>OBLAATELY में अक्षर A दो बार चाहिए, परंतु दिए गए शब्द में A केवल एक बार है, इसलिए यह नहीं बनाया जा सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): OBLAATELY है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Direction: Read the statement carefully and determine which of the given conclusions logically follows.<br><br><b>Statement:</b><br>The retail chain redesigned its mobile application after customer feedback highlighted difficulties in navigation and slow payment processing during online purchases.<br><br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Customers prefer shopping only through mobile applications.<br>II. Problems in navigation and payment processing affected customer experience. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: कथन को ध्यान से पढ़ें और निर्धारित करें कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><br><b>कथन:</b><br>खुदरा श्रृंखला ने अपने मोबाइल ऐप को फिर से डिज़ाइन किया, क्योंकि ग्राहक प्रतिक्रिया ने ऑनलाइन खरीदारी के दौरान नेविगेशन में कठिनाइयों और धीमी भुगतान प्रक्रिया को उजागर किया।<br><br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. ग्राहक केवल मोबाइल ऐप के माध्यम से खरीदारी करना पसंद करते हैं।<br>II. नेविगेशन और भुगतान प्रक्रिया की समस्याओं ने ग्राहक अनुभव को प्रभावित किया। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The app was redesigned because these problems were reported by customers, so they did affect the customer experience. II follows.<br>Nothing in the statement shows a preference for mobile apps only. I does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only II follows.</b>","hi":"ऐप इसलिए फिर से डिज़ाइन किया गया क्योंकि ग्राहकों ने ये समस्याएँ बताईं, अतः इन्होंने ग्राहक अनुभव को प्रभावित किया। II निकलता है।<br>कथन में केवल मोबाइल ऐप पसंद करने का कोई संकेत नहीं। I नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">80</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानें और उसी के अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">80</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"64"},"2":{"en":"36"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"52"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Row-wise: first × second − first = third<br>8 × 11 − 8 = 88 − 8 = 80 ✓<br>5 × 6 − 5 = 30 − 5 = 25 ✓<br>4 × 13 − 4 = 52 − 4 = 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 48.</b>","hi":"पंक्ति-वार: पहला × दूसरा − पहला = तीसरा<br>8 × 11 − 8 = 88 − 8 = 80 ✓<br>5 × 6 − 5 = 30 − 5 = 25 ✓<br>4 × 13 − 4 = 52 − 4 = 48<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002 [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002 [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002"},"2":{"en":"Dr. Sophia J., 15/08/1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002"},"3":{"en":"Dr. Sophia J, 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002"},"4":{"en":"Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600001"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Option (2) changes the date format, option (3) drops the full stop after J and option (4) changes the pin code to 600001.<br>Only option (1) matches the given address letter by letter.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002.</b>","hi":"विकल्प (2) में तिथि का प्रारूप बदल जाता है, विकल्प (3) में J के बाद का पूर्ण विराम हट जाता है और विकल्प (4) में पिन कोड 600001 हो जाता है।<br>केवल विकल्प (1) दिए गए पते से अक्षरशः मेल खाता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Dr. Sophia J., 15-08-1947, Flat-3B, Mount Road, Madras-600002 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which of the given interchanges of signs would make the equation correct?<br>5 + 3 × 8 - 12 ÷ 4 = 3 [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चिह्नों का कौन-सा दिया गया अंतर्परिवर्तन समीकरण को सही बनाएगा?<br>5 + 3 × 8 - 12 ÷ 4 = 3 [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"+ and -","hi":"+ और -"},"2":{"en":"- and ÷","hi":"- और ÷"},"3":{"en":"+ and ×","hi":"+ और ×"},"4":{"en":"× and -","hi":"× और -"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Exchange − and ÷: 5 + 3 × 8 ÷ 12 − 4<br>= 5 + 2 − 4 = 3 ✓<br>The other interchanges do not give 3.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): - and ÷.</b>","hi":"− और ÷ बदलने पर: 5 + 3 × 8 ÷ 12 − 4<br>= 5 + 2 − 4 = 3 ✓<br>शेष अंतर्परिवर्तनों से 3 नहीं आता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): - और ÷ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Before announcing the festival schedule, please confirm the dates with the local authorities.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The announced dates may be incorrect if not confirmed.<br>II. It is important that the public receives accurate information. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान हैं। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>त्योहार का कार्यक्रम घोषित करने से पहले स्थानीय अधिकारियों से तिथियाँ पुष्टि कर लें।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. पुष्टि न होने पर घोषित तिथियाँ गलत हो सकती हैं।<br>II. यह महत्वपूर्ण है कि जनता को सही जानकारी मिले। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The advice to confirm the dates means the dates could otherwise be wrong. I is implicit.<br>Confirmation is asked for so that the public gets correct dates. II is implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"तिथियाँ पुष्टि करने की सलाह का अर्थ है कि अन्यथा तिथियाँ गलत हो सकती हैं। I निहित है।<br>पुष्टि इसलिए कही गई है ताकि जनता को सही तिथियाँ मिलें। II निहित है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): I और II दोनों निहित हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The agriculture department has launched training programs to educate farmers about modern irrigation techniques and efficient water management.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The department believes efficient irrigation can benefit agriculture.<br>II. All farmers currently use outdated farming methods.<br>III. Water management is considered important for agricultural productivity. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानें, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों का खंडन करता प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और निर्धारित करें कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कृषि विभाग ने किसानों को आधुनिक सिंचाई तकनीकों और कुशल जल प्रबंधन के बारे में शिक्षित करने के लिए प्रशिक्षण कार्यक्रम शुरू किए हैं।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. विभाग मानता है कि कुशल सिंचाई कृषि को लाभ पहुँचा सकती है।<br>II. सभी किसान वर्तमान में पुरानी कृषि विधियों का उपयोग करते हैं।<br>III. जल प्रबंधन को कृषि उत्पादकता के लिए महत्वपूर्ण माना जाता है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Only inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II और III निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"All inferences follow.","hi":"सभी अनुमान निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Training is arranged only if modern irrigation is expected to help. I follows.<br>Water management is taught along with it, so it is treated as important for productivity. III follows.<br>The statement does not say that all farmers use outdated methods. II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only inferences I and III follow.</b>","hi":"प्रशिक्षण तभी रखा जाता है जब आधुनिक सिंचाई से लाभ की अपेक्षा हो। I निकलता है।<br>जल प्रबंधन भी उसी के साथ सिखाया जा रहा है, अतः यह उत्पादकता के लिए महत्वपूर्ण माना गया है। III निकलता है।<br>कथन यह नहीं कहता कि सभी किसान पुरानी विधियाँ अपनाते हैं। II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The government reduced import duties on essential raw materials to support domestic manufacturing, even though it may widen the trade deficit in the short term.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The government prioritises domestic manufacturing over short-term trade balance concerns.<br>II. Reduction in import duties always improves the trade balance.<br>III. Domestic manufacturing depends on imported raw materials. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानें, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों का खंडन करता प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और निर्धारित करें कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार ने घरेलू विनिर्माण को सहयोग देने के लिए आवश्यक कच्चे माल पर आयात शुल्क घटाया, भले ही इससे अल्पकाल में व्यापार घाटा बढ़ सकता है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. सरकार अल्पकालिक व्यापार संतुलन की चिंताओं की तुलना में घरेलू विनिर्माण को प्राथमिकता देती है।<br>II. आयात शुल्क में कमी से व्यापार संतुलन सदैव सुधरता है।<br>III. घरेलू विनिर्माण आयातित कच्चे माल पर निर्भर है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only Inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only Inference III follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान III निकलता है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The government accepts a wider trade deficit, which shows manufacturing is the higher priority. I follows.<br>Duties are cut on raw materials used by manufacturers, so manufacturing needs imported raw material. III follows.<br>The statement says the deficit may widen, so II is opposite to the fact given.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Inferences I and III follow.</b>","hi":"सरकार व्यापार घाटा बढ़ने को स्वीकार करती है, जो दर्शाता है कि विनिर्माण को अधिक प्राथमिकता है। I निकलता है।<br>निर्माताओं द्वारा प्रयुक्त कच्चे माल पर शुल्क घटाया गया, अतः विनिर्माण आयातित कच्चे माल पर निर्भर है। III निकलता है।<br>कथन कहता है घाटा बढ़ सकता है, इसलिए II दिए तथ्य के विपरीत है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"During a strategic planning session, a normally composed and highly professional colleague suddenly becomes intensely emotional and visibly defensive when a flaw in their proposal is constructively criticized. The reaction appears heavily disproportionate to the situation, and the room becomes highly uncomfortable.<br><br>What course of action by the group leader demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक रणनीतिक योजना सत्र के दौरान एक सामान्यतः शांत और अत्यधिक पेशेवर सहकर्मी अचानक अत्यधिक भावुक और स्पष्ट रूप से रक्षात्मक हो जाता है जब उसके प्रस्ताव में एक कमी की रचनात्मक आलोचना की जाती है। यह प्रतिक्रिया स्थिति की तुलना में अत्यधिक असंगत लगती है और कक्ष असहज हो जाता है।<br><br>समूह नेता की कौन-सी कार्रवाई भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) का सर्वोच्च स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pretend nothing happened and aggressively push forward with the agenda to stay on schedule.","hi":"कुछ न हुआ हो ऐसा दिखावा करें और समय-सारणी पर बने रहने के लिए आक्रामक रूप से एजेंडा आगे बढ़ाएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Halt the meeting immediately and publicly demand they explain their extreme emotional overreaction.","hi":"बैठक तुरंत रोकें और सार्वजनिक रूप से उनसे उनकी अत्यधिक भावनात्मक प्रतिक्रिया का स्पष्टीकरण माँगें।"},"3":{"en":"Permanently remove the colleague from all future strategic planning assemblies to protect the department.","hi":"विभाग की सुरक्षा के लिए सहकर्मी को भविष्य की सभी रणनीतिक योजना बैठकों से स्थायी रूप से हटा दें।"},"4":{"en":"Briefly acknowledge the tension, maintain a calm environment to finish the meeting, and check in privately later.","hi":"तनाव को संक्षेप में स्वीकारें, बैठक पूरी करने के लिए शांत वातावरण बनाए रखें और बाद में निजी रूप से बात करें।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The reaction points to something personal, so the leader must protect the colleague’s dignity and still finish the work.<br>Option (4) does both; ignoring the issue, publicly questioning or removing the person damages trust.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Briefly acknowledge the tension, maintain a calm environment to finish the meeting, and check in privately later.</b>","hi":"यह प्रतिक्रिया किसी व्यक्तिगत कारण की ओर संकेत करती है, इसलिए नेता को सहकर्मी की गरिमा बचाते हुए काम पूरा करना चाहिए।<br>विकल्प (4) दोनों करता है; अनदेखा करना, सार्वजनिक पूछताछ या हटाना विश्वास को हानि पहुँचाता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): तनाव को संक्षेप में स्वीकारें, बैठक पूरी करने के लिए शांत वातावरण बनाए रखें और बाद में निजी रूप से बात करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Urban Housing Board Allotment:</b><br>(i) Must be a first-time home buyer.<br>(ii) Annual income must be below ₹8 Lakh.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the candidate is not a first-time buyer but the income is below ₹4 Lakh, refer the case to the Board Chairman.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets both criteria (i) and (ii) but is currently residing in a state-sponsored housing unit, refer the case to the Relocation Committee.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate is not a first-time buyer and has an annual income of ₹3 Lakh. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और प्रदान किए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित करें। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू हो, तो वह प्राधिकरण पहचानें जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>शहरी आवास बोर्ड आवंटन के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) प्रथम बार घर खरीदने वाला होना चाहिए।<br>(ii) वार्षिक आय ₹8 लाख से कम होनी चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी प्रथम बार घर खरीदने वाला नहीं है परंतु आय ₹4 लाख से कम है, तो मामला बोर्ड अध्यक्ष को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि अभ्यर्थी दोनों मानदंड (i) और (ii) पूरे करता है परंतु वर्तमान में राज्य प्रायोजित आवास इकाई में निवास कर रहा है, तो मामला पुनर्वास समिति को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> अभ्यर्थी प्रथम बार घर खरीदने वाला नहीं है और उसकी वार्षिक आय ₹3 लाख है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Allotment to be approved","hi":"आवंटन स्वीकृत किया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Board Chairman","hi":"मामला बोर्ड अध्यक्ष को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"Allotment application to be rejected","hi":"आवंटन आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Relocation Committee","hi":"मामला पुनर्वास समिति को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The candidate is not a first-time buyer, so criterion (i) fails.<br>His income ₹3 Lakh is below ₹4 Lakh, so Exception (A) applies.<br>Therefore the case goes to the Board Chairman.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Board Chairman.</b>","hi":"अभ्यर्थी प्रथम बार घर खरीदने वाला नहीं है, इसलिए मानदंड (i) पूरा नहीं होता।<br>उसकी आय ₹3 लाख ₹4 लाख से कम है, इसलिए अपवाद (A) लागू होता है।<br>अतः मामला बोर्ड अध्यक्ष को भेजा जाएगा।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला बोर्ड अध्यक्ष को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some rivers are lakes.<br>Some lakes are seas.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All seas are lakes.<br>II. Some seas are lakes. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन दिए गए हैं और इन कथनों के बाद दो निष्कर्ष हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़ें और फिर निर्धारित करें कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष दिए गए दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ नदियाँ झीलें हैं।<br>कुछ झीलें समुद्र हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी समुद्र झीलें हैं।<br>II. कुछ समुद्र झीलें हैं। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusion I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"“Some lakes are seas” means the seas that are lakes exist, so some seas are lakes. II follows.<br>It does not mean every sea is a lake. I does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"“कुछ झीलें समुद्र हैं” का अर्थ है कि जो समुद्र झीलें हैं वे मौजूद हैं, अतः कुछ समुद्र झीलें हैं। II निकलता है।<br>इसका अर्थ यह नहीं कि हर समुद्र झील है। I नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Direction:<br>Choose the most appropriate course of action.<br><br>An airline must decide whether to continue operating a route that serves remote communities but generates financial losses. The route provides essential connectivity and has limited alternatives. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश:<br>सबसे उपयुक्त कार्यवाही चुनिए।<br><br>एक एयरलाइन को यह तय करना है कि क्या वह उस मार्ग का संचालन जारी रखे जो दूरस्थ समुदायों की सेवा करता है परंतु आर्थिक हानि देता है। यह मार्ग आवश्यक संपर्क प्रदान करता है और इसके विकल्प सीमित हैं। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Discontinue the route because financial performance should be the only criterion.","hi":"मार्ग बंद कर दें क्योंकि आर्थिक प्रदर्शन ही एकमात्र मानदंड होना चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"Continue operating indefinitely without assessing long-term sustainability concerns.","hi":"दीर्घकालिक स्थिरता की चिंताओं का आकलन किए बिना अनिश्चित काल तक संचालन जारी रखें।"},"3":{"en":"Evaluate social value, operational costs, and possible support mechanisms jointly.","hi":"सामाजिक मूल्य, परिचालन लागत और संभावित सहायता तंत्र का संयुक्त रूप से मूल्यांकन करें।"},"4":{"en":"Reduce service frequency immediately without studying passenger requirements.","hi":"यात्री आवश्यकताओं का अध्ययन किए बिना तुरंत सेवा आवृत्ति घटा दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The route is socially necessary but loss-making, so both sides must be weighed before deciding.<br>Option (3) studies value, cost and support together; the others act on a single factor alone.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Evaluate social value, operational costs, and possible support mechanisms jointly.</b>","hi":"मार्ग सामाजिक रूप से आवश्यक है परंतु घाटे में है, इसलिए निर्णय से पहले दोनों पक्षों को तौलना आवश्यक है।<br>विकल्प (3) मूल्य, लागत और सहायता का साथ में अध्ययन करता है; शेष केवल एक कारक पर कार्य करते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): सामाजिक मूल्य, परिचालन लागत और संभावित सहायता तंत्र का संयुक्त रूप से मूल्यांकन करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Public libraries must adopt advanced artificial intelligence systems to manage book inventory and improve user accessibility to rare research materials.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Contemporary library inventory management systems lack the requisite scalability to address the demands of modern data processing.<br>II. The incorporation of artificial intelligence is poised to substantially optimize the research experience for end-users. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़ें। निर्धारित करें कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>पुस्तक सूची के प्रबंधन तथा दुर्लभ शोध सामग्री तक उपयोगकर्ता की पहुँच सुधारने के लिए सार्वजनिक पुस्तकालयों को उन्नत कृत्रिम बुद्धिमत्ता प्रणालियाँ अपनानी चाहिए।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. वर्तमान पुस्तकालय सूची प्रबंधन प्रणालियों में आधुनिक डेटा प्रोसेसिंग की माँगों को पूरा करने योग्य विस्तारशीलता का अभाव है।<br>II. कृत्रिम बुद्धिमत्ता का समावेश अंतिम उपयोगकर्ताओं के शोध अनुभव को पर्याप्त रूप से बेहतर बनाएगा। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Artificial intelligence is recommended because it is expected to improve the users’ research experience. II is implicit.<br>The statement never says that present systems cannot scale, so I is not implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Assumption II is implicit.</b>","hi":"कृत्रिम बुद्धिमत्ता इसलिए सुझाई गई है क्योंकि इससे उपयोगकर्ताओं का शोध अनुभव बेहतर होने की अपेक्षा है। II निहित है।<br>कथन कहीं नहीं कहता कि वर्तमान प्रणालियाँ विस्तार योग्य नहीं हैं, इसलिए I निहित नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल अनुमान II निहित है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"What is the next term in the sequence?<br><br>ZAB, YBC, XCD, WDE, VEF, UFG, ______ [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अनुक्रम में अगला पद क्या है?<br><br>ZAB, YBC, XCD, WDE, VEF, UFG, ______ [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TGH"},"2":{"en":"SGHC"},"3":{"en":"THID"},"4":{"en":"TFG"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letter: Z → Y → X → W → V → U → T (−1 each)<br>Second and third letters: AB → BC → CD → DE → EF → FG → GH (+1 each)<br>Next term = TGH<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): TGH.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर: Z → Y → X → W → V → U → T (प्रत्येक −1)<br>दूसरा और तीसरा अक्षर: AB → BC → CD → DE → EF → FG → GH (प्रत्येक +1)<br>अगला पद = TGH<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): TGH है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In each of the following questions, four options have been given, of which three are alike in some way and one is different. Choose the odd one out. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रत्येक प्रश्न में चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और एक भिन्न है। विषम विकल्प चुनिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Egypt – Cairo","hi":"मिस्र – काहिरा"},"2":{"en":"Kenya – Nairobi","hi":"केन्या – नैरोबी"},"3":{"en":"Nigeria – Lagos","hi":"नाइजीरिया – लागोस"},"4":{"en":"Ethiopia – Addis Ababa","hi":"इथियोपिया – अदिस अबाबा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Cairo, Nairobi and Addis Ababa are the capitals of their countries.<br>Lagos is not the capital of Nigeria — Abuja is — so this pair is different.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Nigeria – Lagos.</b>","hi":"काहिरा, नैरोबी और अदिस अबाबा अपने देशों की राजधानियाँ हैं।<br>लागोस नाइजीरिया की राजधानी नहीं है — अबूजा है — इसलिए यह युग्म भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): नाइजीरिया – लागोस है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070206","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Peninsular Plateau","question":{"en":"The Meghalaya Plateau is geologically considered an extension of which major physiographic division? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मेघालय पठार को भूवैज्ञानिक दृष्टि से किस प्रमुख भौतिक विभाग का विस्तार माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Himalayan Range","hi":"हिमालय श्रेणी"},"2":{"en":"The Peninsular Plateau","hi":"प्रायद्वीपीय पठार"},"3":{"en":"The Indo-Gangetic Plain","hi":"सिंधु-गंगा का मैदान"},"4":{"en":"The Northern Mountains","hi":"उत्तरी पर्वत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The Peninsular Plateau</b><br>The <b>Meghalaya Plateau</b> is geologically an extension of the <b>Peninsular Plateau</b>, separated from the main block by the <b>Garo-Rajmahal gap</b> which was later filled by the sediments of the Ganga and Brahmaputra.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is a part of the <b>Gondwana</b> block and consists of the <b>Garo, Khasi and Jaintia</b> hills.<br>• The plateau is rich in <b>coal, limestone, sillimanite and uranium</b> deposits and receives very heavy rainfall at <b>Mawsynram and Cherrapunji</b>.<br>• The <b>Garo-Rajmahal gap</b> is a structural gap between the Meghalaya Plateau and the Chota Nagpur plateau of the peninsular block.<br>• The plateau is bounded by the <b>Brahmaputra valley</b> in the north and the <b>Barak valley and Bangladesh plains</b> in the south.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – प्रायद्वीपीय पठार</b><br><b>मेघालय पठार</b> भूवैज्ञानिक दृष्टि से <b>प्रायद्वीपीय पठार</b> का विस्तार है, जो मुख्य भाग से <b>गारो-राजमहल अंतराल</b> द्वारा पृथक है; इस अंतराल को बाद में गंगा तथा ब्रह्मपुत्र के अवसादों ने भर दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह <b>गोंडवाना</b> भाग का हिस्सा है तथा <b>गारो, खासी तथा जयंतिया</b> पहाड़ियों से बना है।<br>• यह पठार <b>कोयला, चूना पत्थर, सिलिमेनाइट तथा यूरेनियम</b> के भंडार से समृद्ध है तथा यहाँ <b>मासिनराम एवं चेरापूंजी</b> में अत्यधिक वर्षा होती है।<br>• <b>गारो-राजमहल अंतराल</b> मेघालय पठार तथा प्रायद्वीपीय भाग के छोटा नागपुर पठार के बीच संरचनात्मक अंतराल है।<br>• पठार उत्तर में <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र घाटी</b> तथा दक्षिण में <b>बराक घाटी एवं बांग्लादेश के मैदानों</b> से घिरा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070207","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Whose previous consent is mandatory for the appointment of an ad hoc Judge under Article 127 of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 127 के अंतर्गत तदर्थ न्यायाधीश की नियुक्ति के लिए किसकी पूर्व सहमति अनिवार्य है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Prime Minister of India","hi":"भारत के प्रधानमंत्री"},"2":{"en":"The President of India","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति"},"3":{"en":"The Union Law Minister","hi":"संघ के विधि मंत्री"},"4":{"en":"The Collegium of Supreme Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का कॉलेजियम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The President of India</b><br>Under <b>Article 127</b>, if there is no quorum of judges of the Supreme Court available for a session, the <b>President</b> may appoint <b>ad hoc judges</b>, and this requires the <b>previous consent of the President</b> after consultation with the Chief Justice of India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The appointment is made for the period during which the Court sits, and the ad hoc judge must be a <b>judge of a High Court</b> qualified to be a Supreme Court judge.<br>• <b>Article 128</b> allows the President to appoint <b>retired judges of the Supreme Court or High Courts</b> to sit and act as Supreme Court judges.<br>• <b>Article 124</b> deals with the establishment and constitution of the Supreme Court, and <b>Article 126</b> with the appointment of an <b>acting Chief Justice</b>.<br>• The Supreme Court's strength was raised to <b>34 judges</b> (Chief Justice and 33 others) by an amendment in 2019.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत के राष्ट्रपति</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 127</b> के अंतर्गत यदि सत्र के लिए सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों का गणपूर्ति न हो, तो <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> <b>तदर्थ न्यायाधीश</b> नियुक्त कर सकते हैं और इसके लिए भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश से परामर्श के बाद <b>राष्ट्रपति की पूर्व सहमति</b> आवश्यक होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नियुक्ति उस अवधि के लिए होती है जब तक न्यायालय बैठता है और तदर्थ न्यायाधीश <b>उच्च न्यायालय का न्यायाधीश</b> होना चाहिए जो सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का न्यायाधीश बनने की योग्यता रखता हो।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 128</b> राष्ट्रपति को <b>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय अथवा उच्च न्यायालयों के सेवानिवृत्त न्यायाधीशों</b> को सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश के रूप में बैठने तथा कार्य करने की अनुमति देता है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 124</b> सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की स्थापना एवं गठन से तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 126</b> <b>कार्यवाहक मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> की नियुक्ति से संबंधित है।<br>• 2019 के संशोधन द्वारा सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की संख्या <b>34 न्यायाधीश</b> (मुख्य न्यायाधीश तथा 33 अन्य) की गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070208","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Which physical quantity is represented by the slope of a line on a velocity-time graph? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वेग-समय ग्राफ पर रेखा की प्रवणता किस भौतिक राशि को दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Speed","hi":"चाल"},"2":{"en":"Distance","hi":"दूरी"},"3":{"en":"Acceleration","hi":"त्वरण"},"4":{"en":"Displacement","hi":"विस्थापन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Acceleration</b><br>On a <b>velocity-time graph</b>, the <b>slope</b> gives <b>change in velocity divided by time</b>, which is <b>acceleration</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>straight line</b> in a velocity-time graph means <b>uniform acceleration</b>, and a horizontal line means <b>zero acceleration</b>.<br>• The <b>area under a velocity-time graph</b> gives the <b>displacement</b> covered by the object.<br>• A line bending towards the time axis shows <b>decreasing acceleration</b>, while a steeper line shows greater acceleration.<br>• Acceleration is a <b>vector</b> quantity with SI unit <b>metre per second squared</b>, and it is the rate of change of velocity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – त्वरण</b><br><b>वेग-समय ग्राफ</b> पर <b>प्रवणता</b> <b>वेग में परिवर्तन को समय से भाग</b> देकर प्राप्त होती है, जो <b>त्वरण</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वेग-समय ग्राफ में <b>सरल रेखा</b> <b>एकसमान त्वरण</b> को तथा क्षैतिज रेखा <b>शून्य त्वरण</b> को दर्शाती है।<br>• <b>वेग-समय ग्राफ के नीचे का क्षेत्रफल</b> वस्तु द्वारा तय <b>विस्थापन</b> देता है।<br>• समय अक्ष की ओर मुड़ती रेखा <b>घटता त्वरण</b> तथा अधिक ढाल वाली रेखा अधिक त्वरण दर्शाती है।<br>• त्वरण <b>सदिश</b> राशि है, जिसकी SI इकाई <b>मीटर प्रति सेकंड वर्ग</b> है तथा यह वेग के परिवर्तन की दर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070209","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Force and Laws of Motion","question":{"en":"Which physical reaction occurs in passengers inside a moving bus when it suddenly comes to a halt? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चलती बस के अचानक रुक जाने पर उसमें बैठे यात्रियों में कौन-सी भौतिक प्रतिक्रिया होती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They fall forward abruptly","hi":"वे अचानक आगे गिरते हैं"},"2":{"en":"They fall backwards abruptly","hi":"वे अचानक पीछे गिरते हैं"},"3":{"en":"They move upward abruptly","hi":"वे अचानक ऊपर की ओर जाते हैं"},"4":{"en":"They move sideways abruptly","hi":"वे अचानक बगल की ओर जाते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – They fall forward abruptly</b><br>When the bus stops suddenly, the lower part of the body stops with the bus due to friction, but the upper part continues to move forward because of <b>inertia of motion</b>, so passengers fall <b>forward</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This is a direct consequence of <b>Newton's first law of motion</b>, also called the law of inertia.<br>• <b>Inertia of motion</b> keeps a body moving in the same direction unless an external force acts on it.<br>• When the bus <b>starts suddenly</b>, passengers fall <b>backward</b> due to the <b>inertia of rest</b>.<br>• Seat belts and headrests in vehicles are designed to counter this effect during sudden braking or acceleration.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – वे अचानक आगे गिरते हैं</b><br>बस के अचानक रुकने पर घर्षण के कारण शरीर का निचला भाग बस के साथ रुक जाता है, परंतु ऊपरी भाग <b>गति के जड़त्व</b> के कारण आगे बढ़ता रहता है, अतः यात्री <b>आगे</b> गिरते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह <b>न्यूटन के गति के प्रथम नियम</b> अर्थात जड़त्व के नियम का सीधा परिणाम है।<br>• <b>गति का जड़त्व</b> वस्तु को उसी दिशा में चलते रहने देता है जब तक कोई बाहरी बल कार्य न करे।<br>• बस के <b>अचानक चलने</b> पर <b>विराम के जड़त्व</b> के कारण यात्री <b>पीछे</b> गिरते हैं।<br>• वाहनों में सीट बेल्ट तथा हेडरेस्ट अचानक ब्रेक लगने या त्वरण के समय इस प्रभाव को रोकने हेतु बनाए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070210","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which pulse is also called pigeon pea? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस दलहन को अरहर भी कहा जाता है (अंग्रेजी में pigeon pea)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gram","hi":"चना"},"2":{"en":"Moong","hi":"मूंग"},"3":{"en":"Arhar","hi":"अरहर"},"4":{"en":"Masur","hi":"मसूर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Arhar</b><br><b>Arhar (tur)</b> is the Indian name of <b>pigeon pea</b> (Cajanus cajan), an important <b>kharif pulse</b> grown mainly in Maharashtra, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh and Gujarat.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Arhar</b> is rich in protein, and India is the <b>largest producer and consumer</b> of pulses in the world.<br>• <b>Gram (chana)</b> is Bengal gram or chickpea, <b>moong</b> is green gram and <b>masur</b> is lentil.<br>• Pulses are <b>legumes</b> that fix atmospheric nitrogen in the soil through <b>Rhizobium</b> bacteria in root nodules.<br>• The <b>National Food Security Mission - Pulses</b> and the <b>Pulse Polio</b> analogy are often used in policy discussions on protein security.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अरहर</b><br><b>अरहर (तुअर)</b> <b>pigeon pea</b> का भारतीय नाम है, जो एक महत्वपूर्ण <b>खरीफ दलहन</b> है और मुख्यतः महाराष्ट्र, कर्नाटक, मध्य प्रदेश, उत्तर प्रदेश तथा गुजरात में उगाया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अरहर</b> प्रोटीन से समृद्ध है तथा भारत विश्व में दलहन का <b>सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक एवं उपभोक्ता</b> है।<br>• <b>चना</b> बंगाल ग्राम अथवा चिकपी है, <b>मूंग</b> हरी मूंग तथा <b>मसूर</b> लेंटिल है।<br>• दलहन <b>फलीदार</b> फसलें हैं जो जड़ गांठों में <b>राइजोबियम</b> जीवाणु के माध्यम से वायुमंडलीय नाइट्रोजन का स्थिरीकरण करती हैं।<br>• <b>राष्ट्रीय खाद्य सुरक्षा मिशन - दलहन</b> जैसे कार्यक्रम प्रोटीन सुरक्षा के संदर्भ में चर्चा में रहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070211","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"The provisions relating to anti-defection are contained in which Schedule of the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दल-बदल विरोधी प्रावधान भारतीय संविधान की किस अनुसूची में सम्मिलित हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eighth Schedule","hi":"आठवीं अनुसूची"},"2":{"en":"Ninth Schedule","hi":"नौवीं अनुसूची"},"3":{"en":"Tenth Schedule","hi":"दसवीं अनुसूची"},"4":{"en":"Eleventh Schedule","hi":"ग्यारहवीं अनुसूची"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Tenth Schedule</b><br>The <b>anti-defection law</b> is contained in the <b>Tenth Schedule</b> of the Constitution, added by the <b>52nd Amendment Act, 1985</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A member may be disqualified for <b>voluntarily giving up membership</b> of the party or for <b>voting against the party whip</b>.<br>• The <b>Speaker or Chairman</b> of the House decides disqualification cases, and courts can review the decision only on limited grounds of procedural fairness.<br>• The <b>91st Amendment Act, 2003</b> removed the exemption for a <b>split</b> (one-third of members) and retained only the merger exemption for <b>two-thirds</b> of members.<br>• The <b>Eighth Schedule</b> lists the languages, the <b>Ninth Schedule</b> protects certain laws from judicial review and the <b>Eleventh Schedule</b> deals with Panchayati Raj functions.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – दसवीं अनुसूची</b><br><b>दल-बदल विरोधी कानून</b> संविधान की <b>दसवीं अनुसूची</b> में है, जो <b>52वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1985</b> द्वारा जोड़ा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सदस्य <b>स्वेच्छा से दल की सदस्यता छोड़ने</b> अथवा <b>दल के व्हिप के विरुद्ध मतदान</b> करने पर निरर्हित हो सकता है।<br>• निरर्हता के मामलों का निर्णय <b>अध्यक्ष अथवा सभापति</b> करते हैं तथा न्यायालय केवल प्रक्रियात्मक निष्पक्षता के सीमित आधारों पर पुनरावलोकन कर सकते हैं।<br>• <b>91वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2003</b> ने <b>विभाजन</b> (एक-तिहाई सदस्य) की छूट हटा दी और केवल <b>दो-तिहाई</b> सदस्यों के विलय की छूट रखी।<br>• <b>आठवीं अनुसूची</b> भाषाओं की सूची देती है, <b>नौवीं अनुसूची</b> कुछ कानूनों को न्यायिक पुनरावलोकन से संरक्षण देती है तथा <b>ग्यारहवीं अनुसूची</b> पंचायती राज के कार्यों से संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070212","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following actions is classified as tampering under the doping control regulations? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"डोपिंग नियंत्रण नियमों के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी क्रिया छेड़छाड़ (tampering) के रूप में वर्गीकृत है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Training","hi":"प्रशिक्षण"},"2":{"en":"Bribing","hi":"रिश्वत देना"},"3":{"en":"Coaching","hi":"कोचिंग"},"4":{"en":"Testing","hi":"परीक्षण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bribing</b><br>Under the <b>World Anti-Doping Code</b>, <b>tampering</b> includes <b>bribing officials</b>, altering or destroying samples, and obstructing or intimidating testing personnel.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>WADA Code</b> lists <b>11 anti-doping rule violations</b>, including presence of a prohibited substance, use, refusal to submit a sample, whereabouts failures and trafficking.<br>• <b>Tampering or attempted tampering</b> with any part of doping control is a separate violation, whether or not a prohibited substance is found.<br>• In India, the <b>National Anti-Doping Agency (NADA)</b>, set up in <b>2009</b>, implements anti-doping rules and the <b>National Dope Testing Laboratory</b> carries out testing.<br>• <b>Training, coaching and testing</b> are normal sporting activities and are not violations unless carried out in breach of the rules.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रिश्वत देना</b><br><b>विश्व डोपिंग संहिता</b> के अंतर्गत <b>छेड़छाड़</b> में <b>अधिकारियों को रिश्वत देना</b>, नमूनों को बदलना या नष्ट करना तथा परीक्षण कर्मियों को रोकना या डराना शामिल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>WADA संहिता</b> में <b>11 डोपिंग-विरोधी नियम उल्लंघन</b> दिए गए हैं, जिनमें प्रतिबंधित पदार्थ की उपस्थिति, उपयोग, नमूना देने से इनकार, उपस्थिति संबंधी चूक तथा तस्करी शामिल हैं।<br>• डोपिंग नियंत्रण के किसी भी भाग में <b>छेड़छाड़ या प्रयास</b> पृथक उल्लंघन है, चाहे प्रतिबंधित पदार्थ मिले या न मिले।<br>• भारत में <b>राष्ट्रीय डोपिंग विरोधी एजेंसी (NADA)</b>, जो <b>2009</b> में स्थापित हुई, डोपिंग विरोधी नियम लागू करती है तथा <b>राष्ट्रीय डोप परीक्षण प्रयोगशाला</b> परीक्षण करती है।<br>• <b>प्रशिक्षण, कोचिंग तथा परीक्षण</b> सामान्य खेल गतिविधियाँ हैं और नियमों के उल्लंघन के बिना वे उल्लंघन नहीं हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070213","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which Olympic Games did India achieve its highest-ever total medal count of 7 medals? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस ओलंपिक खेलों में भारत ने 7 पदकों का अपना सर्वाधिक कुल पदक प्राप्त किया? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Beijing 2008","hi":"बीजिंग 2008"},"2":{"en":"London 2012","hi":"लंदन 2012"},"3":{"en":"Tokyo 2020","hi":"टोक्यो 2020"},"4":{"en":"Paris 2024","hi":"पेरिस 2024"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Tokyo 2020</b><br>India won <b>7 medals</b> at the <b>Tokyo 2020 Olympics</b> - <b>1 gold, 2 silver and 4 bronze</b> - its highest total in a single Olympic Games.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won the <b>gold in javelin throw</b>, India's first athletics gold.<br>• <b>Mirabai Chanu</b> won silver in weightlifting, <b>Ravi Dahiya</b> silver in wrestling and the men's hockey team won <b>bronze</b> after 41 years.<br>• Other bronze medallists were <b>P.V. Sindhu, Lovlina Borgohain and Bajrang Punia</b>.<br>• At <b>Paris 2024</b> India won <b>6 medals</b>, and at <b>London 2012</b> it won 6 medals as well.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – टोक्यो 2020</b><br>भारत ने <b>टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक</b> में <b>7 पदक</b> - <b>1 स्वर्ण, 2 रजत तथा 4 कांस्य</b> - जीते, जो एक ओलंपिक में उसका सर्वाधिक कुल पदक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने <b>भाला फेंक में स्वर्ण</b> जीता, जो भारत का पहला एथलेटिक्स स्वर्ण था।<br>• <b>मीराबाई चानू</b> ने भारोत्तोलन में रजत, <b>रवि दहिया</b> ने कुश्ती में रजत तथा पुरुष हॉकी टीम ने 41 वर्ष बाद <b>कांस्य</b> जीता।<br>• अन्य कांस्य पदक विजेता <b>पी.वी. सिंधु, लवलीना बोरगोहेन तथा बजरंग पूनिया</b> थे।<br>• <b>पेरिस 2024</b> में भारत ने <b>6 पदक</b> तथा <b>लंदन 2012</b> में भी 6 पदक जीते थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070214","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Dr. Bhim Singh Bhavesh, who was honoured with the Padma Shri in 2025, is known for his social work in which Indian state? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"डॉ. भीम सिंह भावेश, जिन्हें 2025 में पद्म श्री से सम्मानित किया गया, किस भारतीय राज्य में अपने सामाजिक कार्य के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Bihar","hi":"बिहार"},"3":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Jharkhand","hi":"झारखंड"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bihar</b><br>Dr. <b>Bhim Singh Bhavesh</b> of <b>Bihar</b> was honoured with the <b>Padma Shri in 2025</b> for his social work, especially for the upliftment of the <b>Musahar community</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He founded the <b>Aasha Deep</b> organisation and has worked on education, health and dignity for Dalit and marginalised families.<br>• The <b>Musahar</b> community is one of the most disadvantaged groups in Bihar, and his work has focused on literacy and ending social discrimination.<br>• The <b>Padma Shri</b> is announced every year on the eve of <b>Republic Day</b> and is the fourth-highest civilian award of India.<br>• The <b>Padma awards</b> are given in three categories - <b>Padma Vibhushan, Padma Bhushan and Padma Shri</b> - in fields such as art, literature, science, public affairs and social work.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बिहार</b><br><b>बिहार</b> के डॉ. <b>भीम सिंह भावेश</b> को उनके सामाजिक कार्य, विशेषकर <b>मुसहर समुदाय</b> के उत्थान के लिए <b>2025 में पद्म श्री</b> से सम्मानित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने <b>आशा दीप</b> संस्था की स्थापना की और दलित एवं वंचित परिवारों के लिए शिक्षा, स्वास्थ्य तथा सम्मान के क्षेत्र में कार्य किया।<br>• <b>मुसहर</b> समुदाय बिहार के सर्वाधिक वंचित समूहों में है तथा उनके कार्य ने साक्षरता तथा सामाजिक भेदभाव समाप्त करने पर बल दिया।<br>• <b>पद्म श्री</b> की घोषणा प्रत्येक वर्ष <b>गणतंत्र दिवस</b> की पूर्व संध्या पर होती है और यह भारत का चौथा सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान है।<br>• <b>पद्म पुरस्कार</b> तीन श्रेणियों - <b>पद्म विभूषण, पद्म भूषण तथा पद्म श्री</b> - में कला, साहित्य, विज्ञान, लोक व्यवहार तथा सामाजिक कार्य जैसे क्षेत्रों में दिए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070215","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Heikru Hitongba festival is primarily associated with which of the following events? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हैक्रू हितोंगबा उत्सव मुख्यतः निम्नलिखित में से किस आयोजन से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Traditional boat race","hi":"पारंपरिक नाव दौड़"},"2":{"en":"Flower decoration event","hi":"पुष्प सज्जा आयोजन"},"3":{"en":"Music dance festival","hi":"संगीत नृत्य उत्सव"},"4":{"en":"Harvest food celebration","hi":"फसल भोजन उत्सव"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Traditional boat race</b><br><b>Heikru Hitongba</b> is a traditional <b>boat race festival</b> celebrated in <b>Manipur</b>, held at the <b>Bijoy Govinda Thangapat</b> in Imphal during the month of <b>Ingen</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Groups of rowers compete in long <b>canoes and boats</b>, and the event is dedicated to <b>Lord Vishnu (Bijoy Govinda)</b>.<br>• The festival is associated with the rainy season and is one of the oldest continuing traditions of the Meitei community.<br>• Manipur's other festivals include <b>Yaoshang, Ningol Chakouba, Lai Haraoba, Kang and Sangai Festival</b>.<br>• Other famous Indian boat races are the <b>Vallam Kali of Kerala</b> and the <b>Bhogali Bihu boat races of Assam</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पारंपरिक नाव दौड़</b><br><b>हैक्रू हितोंगबा</b> <b>मणिपुर</b> में मनाया जाने वाला पारंपरिक <b>नाव दौड़ उत्सव</b> है, जो <b>इंगेन</b> माह में इंफाल के <b>विजय गोविंद ठांगपाट</b> पर होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नाविकों के समूह लंबी <b>डोंगी तथा नावों</b> में प्रतिस्पर्धा करते हैं और यह आयोजन <b>भगवान विष्णु (विजय गोविंद)</b> को समर्पित है।<br>• यह उत्सव वर्षा ऋतु से जुड़ा है और मेइतेई समुदाय की सबसे प्राचीन जीवंत परंपराओं में से एक है।<br>• मणिपुर के अन्य उत्सवों में <b>योशांग, निंगोल चाकौबा, लाई हराओबा, कांग तथा संगाई महोत्सव</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• भारत की अन्य प्रसिद्ध नाव दौड़ों में <b>केरल की वल्लम कली</b> तथा <b>असम की भोगाली बिहू नाव दौड़</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070216","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Why is post-collapse continuity rejected in Harappan culture? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हड़प्पा संस्कृति में पतन के बाद निरंतरता क्यों अस्वीकार की जाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cities and script vanished","hi":"नगर तथा लिपि लुप्त हो गए"},"2":{"en":"Kushans invaded immediately","hi":"कुषाणों ने तुरंत आक्रमण किया"},"3":{"en":"North India was abandoned","hi":"उत्तर भारत त्याग दिया गया"},"4":{"en":"Writing evolved smoothly","hi":"लेखन सहज रूप से विकसित हुआ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Cities and script vanished</b><br>The <b>Harappan urban phase</b> was followed by the disappearance of <b>planned cities and the undeciphered script</b>, so archaeologists do not see continuity from the mature Harappan to the later cultures.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• After about <b>1900 BCE</b> the cities declined and people moved to smaller rural settlements, a phase called the <b>Late Harappan or de-urbanisation</b> phase.<br>• Key features that disappeared include <b>grid town planning, standardised weights, seals with script, and large public structures like the Great Bath</b>.<br>• Possible causes of decline include <b>climatic change, drying of rivers, floods, deforestation and decline of trade</b>.<br>• Later cultures such as the <b>Ochre Coloured Pottery, Cemetery H and Jorwe</b> show some regional continuity in pottery but not in urban organisation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नगर तथा लिपि लुप्त हो गए</b><br><b>हड़प्पा नगरीय चरण</b> के बाद <b>नियोजित नगर तथा अपठित लिपि</b> का अंत हो गया, अतः पुरातत्वविद् परिपक्व हड़प्पा से परवर्ती संस्कृतियों तक निरंतरता नहीं देखते।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• लगभग <b>1900 ईसा पूर्व</b> के बाद नगरों का पतन हुआ और लोग छोटी ग्रामीण बस्तियों में चले गए; इस चरण को <b>परवर्ती हड़प्पा अथवा विशहरीकरण</b> कहते हैं।<br>• लुप्त हुई प्रमुख विशेषताओं में <b>ग्रिड नगर नियोजन, मानकीकृत बाट, लिपि युक्त मुहरें तथा विशाल जन-भवन जैसे महान स्नानागार</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• पतन के संभावित कारणों में <b>जलवायु परिवर्तन, नदियों का सूखना, बाढ़, वनों की कटाई तथा व्यापार में गिरावट</b> हैं।<br>• <b>गेरू रंगीन मृदभांड, सिमेट्री एच तथा जोरवे</b> जैसी परवर्ती संस्कृतियों में मृदभांड की क्षेत्रीय निरंतरता दिखती है, परंतु नगरीय संगठन की नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070217","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"What is the designation of Parvathaneni Harish in 2026, who made headlines in 2025 for advocating India's stance on United Nations Security Council (UNSC) reforms at the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2026 में पार्वथनेनी हरीश का पदनाम क्या है, जिन्होंने 2025 में संयुक्त राष्ट्र महासभा (UNGA) में संयुक्त राष्ट्र सुरक्षा परिषद (UNSC) सुधारों पर भारत के रुख का समर्थन करते हुए सुर्खियाँ बटोरीं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Foreign Secretary of India","hi":"भारत के विदेश सचिव"},"2":{"en":"Ambassador of India to the United States","hi":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका में भारत के राजदूत"},"3":{"en":"Permanent Representative of India to the United Nations","hi":"संयुक्त राष्ट्र में भारत के स्थायी प्रतिनिधि"},"4":{"en":"High Commissioner of India to the United Kingdom","hi":"यूनाइटेड किंगडम में भारत के उच्चायुक्त"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Permanent Representative of India to the United Nations</b><br><b>Parvathaneni Harish</b> is the <b>Permanent Representative of India to the United Nations</b> in New York and spoke in the <b>UNGA</b> on India's demand for <b>UNSC reforms</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India is a member of the <b>G4 group</b> with <b>Brazil, Germany and Japan</b>, which seeks permanent seats in a reformed Security Council.<br>• India has been elected to the UN Security Council as a <b>non-permanent member for eight terms</b>, the latest being <b>2021-22</b>.<br>• Reforms sought include <b>expansion in both permanent and non-permanent categories</b> and improvement in the Council's working methods.<br>• The <b>Permanent Mission of India to the UN</b> is located in New York, and the Ambassador also represents India at the <b>UNGA</b> and other UN bodies.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संयुक्त राष्ट्र में भारत के स्थायी प्रतिनिधि</b><br><b>पार्वथनेनी हरीश</b> न्यूयॉर्क में <b>संयुक्त राष्ट्र में भारत के स्थायी प्रतिनिधि</b> हैं और उन्होंने <b>UNGA</b> में <b>UNSC सुधार</b> की भारत की माँग पर बात रखी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत <b>ब्राजील, जर्मनी तथा जापान</b> के साथ <b>G4 समूह</b> का सदस्य है, जो सुधारित सुरक्षा परिषद में स्थायी सीट चाहता है।<br>• भारत <b>आठ बार</b> संयुक्त राष्ट्र सुरक्षा परिषद का <b>अस्थायी सदस्य</b> निर्वाचित हुआ है, जिसमें नवीनतम अवधि <b>2021-22</b> थी।<br>• माँगे जा रहे सुधारों में <b>स्थायी तथा अस्थायी दोनों श्रेणियों में विस्तार</b> तथा परिषद की कार्यप्रणाली में सुधार शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>संयुक्त राष्ट्र में भारत का स्थायी मिशन</b> न्यूयॉर्क में है तथा राजदूत <b>UNGA</b> एवं अन्य संयुक्त राष्ट्र निकायों में भारत का प्रतिनिधित्व करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070218","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Under the MISHTI (Mangrove Initiative for Shoreline Habitats & Tangible Incomes) initiative, which resource is prioritized for conservation and plantation along India's shoreline? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"MISHTI (मैंग्रोव इनिशिएटिव फॉर शोरलाइन हैबिटेट्स एंड टेंजिबल इनकम्स) पहल के अंतर्गत भारत की तटरेखा पर संरक्षण तथा वृक्षारोपण के लिए किस संसाधन को प्राथमिकता दी जाती है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Medicinal herbs in the Himalayas","hi":"हिमालय की औषधीय जड़ी-बूटियाँ"},"2":{"en":"Mangroves along India's coastline","hi":"भारत की तटरेखा पर मैंग्रोव"},"3":{"en":"Sandalwood trees in Southern India","hi":"दक्षिण भारत के चंदन वृक्ष"},"4":{"en":"Bamboo clusters in the North East","hi":"पूर्वोत्तर के बाँस समूह"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Mangroves along India's coastline</b><br><b>MISHTI</b> focuses on <b>mangrove conservation and plantation</b> along India's coastline, and was announced in the Union Budget of <b>2023-24</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme aims at <b>mangrove plantation along the coastline and on salt pan lands</b> over five years, using the <b>MGNREGA</b> and <b>CAMPA</b> funds.<br>• Mangroves act as <b>natural barriers against cyclones and storm surges</b>, prevent coastal erosion and support fisheries and local livelihoods.<br>• India has mangrove cover of about <b>4,990 square kilometres</b>, with major areas in the <b>Sundarbans, Bhitarkanika, Godavari-Krishna delta and Gulf of Kachchh</b>.<br>• Other budget announcements of 2023-24 for the environment were <b>Amrit Dharohar</b> for wetlands and the <b>Green Credit Programme</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत की तटरेखा पर मैंग्रोव</b><br><b>MISHTI</b> भारत की तटरेखा पर <b>मैंग्रोव संरक्षण तथा वृक्षारोपण</b> पर केंद्रित है और इसकी घोषणा <b>2023-24</b> के केंद्रीय बजट में हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना का उद्देश्य पाँच वर्षों में <b>तटरेखा तथा लवणीय भूमि पर मैंग्रोव रोपण</b> है, जिसके लिए <b>मनरेगा</b> तथा <b>CAMPA</b> निधियों का उपयोग होता है।<br>• मैंग्रोव <b>चक्रवातों एवं तूफानी उछाल के विरुद्ध प्राकृतिक अवरोध</b> का कार्य करते हैं, तटीय अपरदन रोकते हैं तथा मत्स्य पालन एवं स्थानीय आजीविका को सहारा देते हैं।<br>• भारत में मैंग्रोव आवरण लगभग <b>4,990 वर्ग किलोमीटर</b> है, जिसके प्रमुख क्षेत्र <b>सुंदरबन, भितरकनिका, गोदावरी-कृष्णा डेल्टा तथा कच्छ की खाड़ी</b> हैं।<br>• 2023-24 के बजट में पर्यावरण हेतु <b>अमृत धरोहर</b> (आर्द्रभूमि) तथा <b>हरित ऋण कार्यक्रम</b> की भी घोषणा हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070219","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the daily stipend provided during the training period under the PM Vishwakarma Scheme in India? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में पीएम विश्वकर्मा योजना के अंतर्गत प्रशिक्षण अवधि के दौरान प्रतिदिन कितना वजीफा दिया जाता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"200 rupees per day","hi":"200 रुपये प्रतिदिन"},"2":{"en":"500 rupees per day","hi":"500 रुपये प्रतिदिन"},"3":{"en":"750 rupees per day","hi":"750 रुपये प्रतिदिन"},"4":{"en":"1,000 rupees per day","hi":"1,000 रुपये प्रतिदिन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 500 rupees per day</b><br>Under the <b>PM Vishwakarma Scheme</b>, a <b>stipend of 500 rupees per day</b> is given to artisans and craftspeople during the <b>training period</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme was launched on <b>17 September 2023</b> with an outlay of about <b>13,000 crore rupees</b> for <b>18 traditional trades</b> such as carpenter, blacksmith, potter, tailor and barber.<br>• It provides <b>skill training with a stipend</b>, <b>toolkit incentives of 15,000 rupees</b>, <b>collateral-free credit support</b> of 1 lakh and 2 lakh rupees, and <b>digital transaction and marketing support</b>.<br>• The scheme is implemented by the <b>Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises</b>.<br>• Beneficiaries are given a <b>PM Vishwakarma certificate and identity card</b>, and the scheme also provides <b>life and accident insurance</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 500 रुपये प्रतिदिन</b><br><b>पीएम विश्वकर्मा योजना</b> के अंतर्गत <b>प्रशिक्षण अवधि</b> के दौरान शिल्पकारों तथा कारीगरों को <b>500 रुपये प्रतिदिन का वजीफा</b> दिया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना <b>17 सितंबर 2023</b> को लगभग <b>13,000 करोड़ रुपये</b> के परिव्यय के साथ <b>18 पारंपरिक व्यवसायों</b> जैसे बढ़ई, लोहार, कुम्हार, दर्जी तथा नाई के लिए शुरू की गई।<br>• इसमें <b>वजीफे के साथ कौशल प्रशिक्षण</b>, <b>15,000 रुपये का टूलकिट प्रोत्साहन</b>, <b>1 लाख तथा 2 लाख रुपये की बिना जमानत ऋण सहायता</b> तथा <b>डिजिटल लेनदेन एवं विपणन सहायता</b> दी जाती है।<br>• योजना <b>सूक्ष्म, लघु एवं मध्यम उद्यम मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा क्रियान्वित होती है।<br>• लाभार्थियों को <b>पीएम विश्वकर्मा प्रमाण पत्र तथा पहचान पत्र</b> दिया जाता है और योजना <b>जीवन एवं दुर्घटना बीमा</b> भी प्रदान करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070220","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"The term \"BRIC\", referring to Brazil, Russia, India, and China as major emerging economies, was originally coined by: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"BRIC\" शब्द, जो ब्राजील, रूस, भारत तथा चीन को प्रमुख उभरती अर्थव्यवस्थाओं के रूप में संदर्भित करता है, मूल रूप से किसने गढ़ा था? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jim O'Neill","hi":"जिम ओ'नील"},"2":{"en":"Joseph Stiglitz","hi":"जोसेफ स्टिग्लिट्ज"},"3":{"en":"Nouriel Roubini","hi":"नूरियल रूबिनी"},"4":{"en":"Jeffrey Sachs","hi":"जेफ्री सैक्स"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Jim O'Neill</b><br>The term <b>BRIC</b> was coined by <b>Jim O'Neill</b>, then chief economist at <b>Goldman Sachs</b>, in a paper published in <b>2001</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The grouping became <b>BRICS</b> in <b>2010</b> when <b>South Africa</b> joined, and it expanded further with new members in <b>2024 and 2025</b>.<br>• BRICS works through the <b>New Development Bank</b> and the <b>Contingent Reserve Arrangement</b>, aimed at financing infrastructure and providing financial safety.<br>• Summits are held annually, and the <b>2023 summit at Johannesburg</b> decided to invite new members.<br>• <b>Joseph Stiglitz</b> and <b>Jeffrey Sachs</b> are noted economists, and <b>Nouriel Roubini</b> is known as \"Dr. Doom\" for predicting the 2008 crisis.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जिम ओ'नील</b><br><b>BRIC</b> शब्द <b>जिम ओ'नील</b> ने गढ़ा था, जो उस समय <b>गोल्डमैन सैक्स</b> के मुख्य अर्थशास्त्री थे, और यह <b>2001</b> में प्रकाशित एक पत्र में आया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>2010</b> में <b>दक्षिण अफ्रीका</b> के जुड़ने पर समूह <b>BRICS</b> बना और <b>2024 तथा 2025</b> में इसमें नए सदस्य जुड़े।<br>• BRICS <b>नई विकास बैंक</b> तथा <b>आकस्मिक आरक्षित व्यवस्था</b> के माध्यम से कार्य करता है, जिनका उद्देश्य अवसंरचना वित्तपोषण तथा वित्तीय सुरक्षा प्रदान करना है।<br>• शिखर सम्मेलन प्रतिवर्ष होते हैं तथा <b>जोहान्सबर्ग 2023 शिखर सम्मेलन</b> में नए सदस्यों को आमंत्रित करने का निर्णय हुआ।<br>• <b>जोसेफ स्टिग्लिट्ज</b> तथा <b>जेफ्री सैक्स</b> प्रसिद्ध अर्थशास्त्री हैं तथा <b>नूरियल रूबिनी</b> 2008 के संकट की भविष्यवाणी के कारण \"डॉ. डूम\" कहे जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070221","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A was earlier convicted under Chapter XVII with imprisonment for 4 years. After release, A again commits another offence under the same chapter punishable with imprisonment for 4 years. Which of the following is legally correct under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A पूर्व में अध्याय XVII के अंतर्गत 4 वर्ष के कारावास से दोषसिद्ध हुआ था। रिहा होने के बाद A उसी अध्याय के अंतर्गत एक और अपराध करता है जिसमें 4 वर्ष का कारावास दंडनीय है। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A must necessarily be sentenced to life imprisonment.","hi":"A को अनिवार्यतः आजीवन कारावास का दंड दिया जाएगा।"},"2":{"en":"A cannot be sentenced beyond 4 years because punishment cannot exceed that prescribed for the offence.","hi":"A को 4 वर्ष से अधिक दंड नहीं दिया जा सकता क्योंकि दंड अपराध के लिए निर्धारित दंड से अधिक नहीं हो सकता।"},"3":{"en":"A becomes liable to either life imprisonment or imprisonment up to 10 years.","hi":"A आजीवन कारावास अथवा 10 वर्ष तक के कारावास का दंडनीय हो जाता है।"},"4":{"en":"The previous conviction is irrelevant unless both offences are identical.","hi":"पूर्व दोषसिद्धि अप्रासंगिक है जब तक दोनों अपराध समान न हों।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A becomes liable to either life imprisonment or imprisonment up to 10 years</b><br>Where a person is <b>again convicted</b> of an offence under the same chapter within the specified period, the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> provides an <b>enhanced punishment</b>, so A becomes liable to <b>life imprisonment or imprisonment up to 10 years</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chapter <b>XVII</b> of the BNS deals with offences against <b>property</b>, such as theft, robbery, dacoity and criminal misappropriation.<br>• The provision on <b>repeat conviction</b> is designed as a deterrent and overrides the ordinary maximum punishment prescribed for the substantive offence.<br>• Enhanced punishment provisions exist for <b>habitual offenders</b> and persons convicted more than once within the statutory period.<br>• The BNS replaced the <b>Indian Penal Code, 1860</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>, along with the BNSS and the BSA.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – A आजीवन कारावास अथवा 10 वर्ष तक के कारावास का दंडनीय हो जाता है।</b><br>जब कोई व्यक्ति निर्धारित अवधि में उसी अध्याय के अंतर्गत <b>पुनः दोषसिद्ध</b> होता है, तो <b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> <b>वर्धित दंड</b> का प्रावधान करती है, अतः A <b>आजीवन कारावास अथवा 10 वर्ष तक के कारावास</b> का दंडनीय हो जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNS का अध्याय <b>XVII</b> <b>संपत्ति के विरुद्ध अपराधों</b> से संबंधित है, जैसे चोरी, लूट, डकैती तथा आपराधिक अभिग्रहण।<br>• <b>पुनः दोषसिद्धि</b> का प्रावधान निवारक उद्देश्य से है और यह मूल अपराध के लिए निर्धारित सामान्य अधिकतम दंड पर प्रभावी होता है।<br>• <b>आदतन अपराधियों</b> तथा सांविधिक अवधि में एक से अधिक बार दोषसिद्ध व्यक्तियों के लिए वर्धित दंड के प्रावधान हैं।<br>• BNS ने <b>भारतीय दंड संहिता, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया और यह BNSS तथा BSA के साथ <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070222","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A statute authorizes a \"magistrate\" to suspend licences for public safety reasons. The function is purely administrative and involves no adjudication of guilt or appreciation of evidence. Under Section 3 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India, who should ordinarily exercise this power? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक विधि \"मजिस्ट्रेट\" को लोक सुरक्षा के कारणों से लाइसेंस निलंबित करने का अधिकार देती है। यह कार्य पूर्णतः प्रशासनिक है और इसमें दोष का निर्णय अथवा साक्ष्य का मूल्यांकन सम्मिलित नहीं है। भारत में भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 की धारा 3 के अंतर्गत यह शक्ति सामान्यतः कौन प्रयोग करेगा? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Judicial magistrate only","hi":"केवल न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट"},"2":{"en":"Executive magistrate only","hi":"केवल कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट"},"3":{"en":"High Court","hi":"उच्च न्यायालय"},"4":{"en":"Police Commissioner automatically","hi":"स्वतः पुलिस आयुक्त"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Executive magistrate only</b><br>Under <b>Section 3 of the BNSS, 2023</b>, where the function is <b>purely administrative</b> and involves <b>no adjudication of guilt or appreciation of evidence</b>, the powers of a magistrate are exercised by an <b>Executive Magistrate</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The BNSS classifies magisterial functions into <b>judicial functions</b>, to be exercised by Judicial Magistrates, and <b>administrative or executive functions</b>, to be exercised by Executive Magistrates.<br>• <b>Executive Magistrates</b> include the District Magistrate, Sub-divisional Magistrate and Special Executive Magistrates appointed by the State Government.<br>• <b>Judicial Magistrates</b> deal with trial of offences, bail, remand and appreciation of evidence, while executive magistrates handle <b>public order, licensing and preventive action</b>.<br>• The separation of judicial and executive magistracy follows the <b>separation of powers</b> principle reflected in Articles 50 and 246 of the Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट</b><br><b>BNSS, 2023 की धारा 3</b> के अंतर्गत जहाँ कार्य <b>पूर्णतः प्रशासनिक</b> है और उसमें <b>दोष का निर्णय अथवा साक्ष्य का मूल्यांकन</b> सम्मिलित नहीं है, वहाँ मजिस्ट्रेट की शक्तियाँ <b>कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट</b> प्रयोग करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNSS मजिस्ट्रेटी कार्यों को <b>न्यायिक कार्यों</b>, जिन्हें न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट करते हैं, तथा <b>प्रशासनिक अथवा कार्यपालक कार्यों</b>, जिन्हें कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट करते हैं, में विभाजित करती है।<br>• <b>कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट</b> में जिला मजिस्ट्रेट, उप-प्रभागीय मजिस्ट्रेट तथा राज्य सरकार द्वारा नियुक्त विशेष कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>न्यायिक मजिस्ट्रेट</b> अपराधों के विचारण, जमानत, रिमांड तथा साक्ष्य मूल्यांकन का कार्य करते हैं, जबकि कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट <b>लोक व्यवस्था, लाइसेंसिंग तथा निवारक कार्रवाई</b> करते हैं।<br>• न्यायिक तथा कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेटी का पृथक्करण संविधान के अनुच्छेद 50 तथा 246 में परिलक्षित <b>शक्तियों के पृथक्करण</b> सिद्धांत का अनुसरण करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070223","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Who is recognized as India's first female elephant mahout? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत की पहली महिला हाथी महावत (महूत) के रूप में किसे मान्यता प्राप्त है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Parbati Baruah","hi":"पार्वती बरुआ"},"2":{"en":"Rupa Bai","hi":"रूपा बाई"},"3":{"en":"Velliyamma","hi":"वेल्लियम्मा"},"4":{"en":"Sudha Murthy","hi":"सुधा मूर्ति"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Parbati Baruah</b><br><b>Parbati Baruah</b> of <b>Assam</b> is recognised as India's <b>first female elephant mahout</b> and is known for taming wild elephants and for her work on human-elephant conflict.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She was awarded the <b>Padma Shri in 2024</b> for her contribution to elephant conservation and was the first woman to receive the <b>Gaon Burha</b> title in Assam.<br>• A <b>mahout</b> is a person who trains, rides and cares for an elephant, traditionally a male occupation.<br>• She has worked to reduce <b>human-elephant conflict</b> in Assam and has campaigned for the welfare of captive elephants.<br>• The <b>Asian elephant</b> is India's national heritage animal and is listed as <b>Endangered</b> in the IUCN Red List.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – पार्वती बरुआ</b><br><b>असम</b> की <b>पार्वती बरुआ</b> भारत की <b>पहली महिला हाथी महावत</b> के रूप में मान्यता प्राप्त हैं और जंगली हाथियों को साधने तथा मानव-हाथी संघर्ष पर कार्य के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• हाथी संरक्षण में योगदान के लिए उन्हें <b>2024 में पद्म श्री</b> से सम्मानित किया गया तथा वे असम में <b>गाँव बुढ़ा</b> उपाधि पाने वाली पहली महिला थीं।<br>• <b>महावत</b> वह व्यक्ति होता है जो हाथी को प्रशिक्षित करता है, उस पर सवारी करता है तथा उसकी देखभाल करता है; परंपरागत रूप से यह पुरुषों का व्यवसाय था।<br>• उन्होंने असम में <b>मानव-हाथी संघर्ष</b> घटाने तथा बंदी हाथियों के कल्याण के लिए कार्य किया है।<br>• <b>एशियाई हाथी</b> भारत का राष्ट्रीय धरोहर पशु है और IUCN लाल सूची में <b>संकटग्रस्त</b> श्रेणी में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070224","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: National News","question":{"en":"Which Wildlife Sanctuary hosted the national-level celebration of World Wetlands Day 2026? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस 2026 के राष्ट्रीय स्तर के आयोजन की मेजबानी किस वन्यजीव अभयारण्य ने की? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Asola Bhatti Wildlife Sanctuary","hi":"असोला भट्टी वन्यजीव अभयारण्य"},"2":{"en":"Burachapori Wildlife Sanctuary","hi":"बुराचापोरी वन्यजीव अभयारण्य"},"3":{"en":"Gir Wildlife Sanctuary","hi":"गिर वन्यजीव अभयारण्य"},"4":{"en":"Kaimur Wildlife Sanctuary","hi":"कैमूर वन्यजीव अभयारण्य"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Asola Bhatti Wildlife Sanctuary</b><br>The <b>national-level celebration of World Wetlands Day 2026</b> was hosted at the <b>Asola Bhatti Wildlife Sanctuary</b> in Delhi.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>World Wetlands Day</b> is celebrated on <b>2 February</b>, marking the adoption of the <b>Ramsar Convention on Wetlands in 1971</b> in Iran.<br>• The <b>Asola Bhatti Wildlife Sanctuary</b> lies on the <b>Delhi-Haryana Aravalli ridge</b> and contains the <b>Bhatti mines</b> area with wetland habitats.<br>• India has over <b>90 Ramsar sites</b>, the largest network in Asia, and the theme for World Wetlands Day 2026 relates to <b>wetland restoration</b>.<br>• <b>Gir</b> in Gujarat is famous for Asiatic lions, <b>Burachapori</b> in Assam for grasslands and rhinos, and <b>Kaimur</b> in Bihar for its forests.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – असोला भट्टी वन्यजीव अभयारण्य</b><br><b>विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस 2026</b> का राष्ट्रीय स्तर का आयोजन दिल्ली के <b>असोला भट्टी वन्यजीव अभयारण्य</b> में हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस</b> <b>2 फरवरी</b> को मनाया जाता है, जो 1971 में ईरान में <b>आर्द्रभूमि पर रामसर अभिसमय</b> के अंगीकरण का स्मरण है।<br>• <b>असोला भट्टी वन्यजीव अभयारण्य</b> <b>दिल्ली-हरियाणा अरावली श्रेणी</b> पर स्थित है और इसमें <b>भट्टी खान</b> क्षेत्र की आर्द्रभूमियाँ सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• भारत में <b>90 से अधिक रामसर स्थल</b> हैं, जो एशिया का सबसे बड़ा नेटवर्क है, तथा विश्व आर्द्रभूमि दिवस 2026 की थीम <b>आर्द्रभूमि पुनर्स्थापन</b> से संबंधित है।<br>• गुजरात का <b>गिर</b> एशियाई सिंहों के लिए, असम का <b>बुराचापोरी</b> घास के मैदानों एवं गैंडों के लिए तथा बिहार का <b>कैमूर</b> अपने वनों के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070225","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which structural change in the sectoral composition of India's national income is most consistent with the post-1991 reform period? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत की राष्ट्रीय आय की क्षेत्रीय संरचना में कौन-सा संरचनात्मक परिवर्तन 1991 के बाद के सुधार काल से सर्वाधिक संगत है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Decline in industry's and services' shares, rise in agriculture's share","hi":"उद्योग तथा सेवाओं की हिस्सेदारी में कमी, कृषि की हिस्सेदारी में वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Equalisation of agriculture's, industry's, and services' shares","hi":"कृषि, उद्योग तथा सेवाओं की हिस्सेदारियों का समान होना"},"3":{"en":"Rise in agriculture's share, decline in industry's and services' shares","hi":"कृषि की हिस्सेदारी में वृद्धि, उद्योग तथा सेवाओं की हिस्सेदारी में कमी"},"4":{"en":"Decline in agriculture's share, rise in industry and services","hi":"कृषि की हिस्सेदारी में कमी, उद्योग तथा सेवाओं की हिस्सेदारी में वृद्धि"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Decline in agriculture's share, rise in industry and services</b><br>After the <b>1991 reforms</b>, the share of <b>agriculture</b> in national income <b>declined</b> steadily, while the shares of <b>industry and especially services</b> <b>rose</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Services now account for more than <b>half of India's gross value added</b>, while agriculture's share has fallen to around <b>one-sixth</b>.<br>• The growth of <b>IT, telecommunications, banking and trade</b> after liberalisation drove the expansion of the service sector.<br>• This pattern is called <b>structural transformation</b>, though in India it has been <b>services-led</b> rather than manufacturing-led.<br>• The share of <b>manufacturing</b> in GDP has remained roughly stagnant at about <b>17%</b>, which is a concern for employment generation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – कृषि की हिस्सेदारी में कमी, उद्योग तथा सेवाओं की हिस्सेदारी में वृद्धि</b><br><b>1991 के सुधारों</b> के बाद राष्ट्रीय आय में <b>कृषि</b> की हिस्सेदारी लगातार <b>घटी</b>, जबकि <b>उद्योग तथा विशेषकर सेवाओं</b> की हिस्सेदारी <b>बढ़ी</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सेवाएँ अब भारत के <b>सकल मूल्य वर्धन के आधे से अधिक</b> का योगदान देती हैं, जबकि कृषि की हिस्सेदारी लगभग <b>छठे भाग</b> तक घट गई है।<br>• उदारीकरण के बाद <b>आईटी, दूरसंचार, बैंकिंग तथा व्यापार</b> की वृद्धि ने सेवा क्षेत्र का विस्तार किया।<br>• इस प्रवृत्ति को <b>संरचनात्मक रूपांतरण</b> कहते हैं, यद्यपि भारत में यह विनिर्माण के स्थान पर <b>सेवा-नेतृत्व</b> वाला रहा।<br>• सकल घरेलू उत्पाद में <b>विनिर्माण</b> की हिस्सेदारी लगभग <b>17%</b> पर लगभग स्थिर रही है, जो रोजगार सृजन के लिए चिंता का विषय है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070226","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"What does the Business Reforms Action Plan (BRAP) framework primarily encourage States and Union Territories to do? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना (BRAP) ढाँचा मुख्य रूप से राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों को क्या करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Restrict investments by imposing additional regulatory controls","hi":"अतिरिक्त नियामक नियंत्रण लगाकर निवेश को सीमित करना"},"2":{"en":"Increase business compliance costs by introducing more procedures","hi":"अधिक प्रक्रियाएँ लाकर व्यापार अनुपालन लागत बढ़ाना"},"3":{"en":"Avoid adopting digital systems for delivering regulatory services","hi":"नियामक सेवाएँ देने के लिए डिजिटल प्रणाली अपनाने से बचना"},"4":{"en":"Promote competitive federalism by implementing business regulatory reforms","hi":"व्यापार नियामक सुधार लागू कर प्रतिस्पर्धी संघवाद को बढ़ावा देना"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Promote competitive federalism by implementing business regulatory reforms</b><br>The <b>BRAP framework</b> encourages States and Union Territories to carry out business regulatory reforms and ranks them, thereby promoting <b>competitive federalism</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BRAP is coordinated by the <b>Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT)</b> and began in <b>2014</b>.<br>• States are assessed on <b>single-window clearance, online service delivery, land and construction permits, labour regulation and dispute resolution</b>.<br>• The rankings create incentives for States to <b>reduce compliance burden, adopt digital governance and attract investment</b>.<br>• It complements other initiatives such as the <b>National Single Window System, Jan Vishwas Act and decriminalisation of minor offences</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – व्यापार नियामक सुधार लागू कर प्रतिस्पर्धी संघवाद को बढ़ावा देना</b><br><b>BRAP ढाँचा</b> राज्यों तथा केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों को व्यापार नियामक सुधार करने के लिए प्रोत्साहित करता है और उन्हें रैंक करता है, जिससे <b>प्रतिस्पर्धी संघवाद</b> को बढ़ावा मिलता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BRAP का समन्वय <b>उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग (DPIIT)</b> करता है और यह <b>2014</b> में आरंभ हुआ।<br>• राज्यों का आकलन <b>एकल खिड़की मंजूरी, ऑनलाइन सेवा वितरण, भूमि तथा निर्माण अनुमतियाँ, श्रम नियमन एवं विवाद समाधान</b> पर होता है।<br>• रैंकिंग राज्यों को <b>अनुपालन बोझ घटाने, डिजिटल शासन अपनाने तथा निवेश आकर्षित करने</b> हेतु प्रोत्साहन देती है।<br>• यह <b>राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली, जन विश्वास अधिनियम तथा लघु अपराधों का अपराधीकरण हटाने</b> जैसी पहलों का पूरक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070227","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"According to the World Happiness Report 2026, how many countries recorded statistically significant gains in life evaluation between the 2006-2010 base period and 2023-2025? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026 के अनुसार, 2006-2010 की आधार अवधि तथा 2023-2025 के बीच कितने देशों ने जीवन मूल्यांकन में सांख्यिकीय रूप से महत्वपूर्ण वृद्धि दर्ज की? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"136"},"2":{"en":"21"},"3":{"en":"41"},"4":{"en":"79"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 79</b><br>According to the <b>World Happiness Report 2026</b>, <b>79 countries</b> recorded statistically significant gains in <b>life evaluation</b> between the <b>2006-2010</b> base period and <b>2023-2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>World Happiness Report</b> is published by the <b>Wellbeing Research Centre, University of Oxford</b>, in partnership with <b>Gallup</b> and the UN Sustainable Development Solutions Network.<br>• It ranks countries on <b>life evaluation</b> measured by the <b>Cantril ladder</b>, along with factors such as GDP per capita, social support, healthy life expectancy, freedom, generosity and perceptions of corruption.<br>• <b>Finland</b> has topped the ranking for several consecutive years, while India ranks low among the countries surveyed.<br>• The report is released every year around the <b>International Day of Happiness on 20 March</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 79</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026</b> के अनुसार <b>79 देशों</b> ने <b>2006-2010</b> की आधार अवधि तथा <b>2023-2025</b> के बीच <b>जीवन मूल्यांकन</b> में सांख्यिकीय रूप से महत्वपूर्ण वृद्धि दर्ज की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट</b> <b>ऑक्सफोर्ड विश्वविद्यालय के वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर</b> द्वारा <b>गैलप</b> तथा संयुक्त राष्ट्र सतत विकास समाधान नेटवर्क के सहयोग से प्रकाशित होती है।<br>• यह देशों को <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> से मापे गए <b>जीवन मूल्यांकन</b> के आधार पर रैंक करती है, साथ ही प्रति व्यक्ति जीडीपी, सामाजिक सहायता, स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा, स्वतंत्रता, उदारता तथा भ्रष्टाचार की धारणा जैसे कारक भी देखे जाते हैं।<br>• <b>फिनलैंड</b> लगातार कई वर्षों से सूची में शीर्ष पर रहा है, जबकि सर्वेक्षण किए गए देशों में भारत का स्थान निम्न है।<br>• यह रिपोर्ट प्रतिवर्ष <b>20 मार्च को अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रसन्नता दिवस</b> के आसपास जारी होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070228","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"According to the World Happiness Report 2026, which factor was associated with a greater improvement in life satisfaction than reducing social media use among girls in the United Kingdom and Ireland? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026 के अनुसार, यूनाइटेड किंगडम तथा आयरलैंड की लड़कियों में सोशल मीडिया के उपयोग को घटाने की तुलना में जीवन संतुष्टि में अधिक सुधार किस कारक से जुड़ा था? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increased physical exercise","hi":"शारीरिक व्यायाम में वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Greater school belonging","hi":"विद्यालय से अधिक जुड़ाव"},"3":{"en":"Higher household income","hi":"अधिक घरेलू आय"},"4":{"en":"Urban residence","hi":"शहरी निवास"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Greater school belonging</b><br>The <b>World Happiness Report 2026</b> found that a sense of <b>school belonging</b> was associated with a <b>greater improvement in life satisfaction</b> among girls in the <b>United Kingdom and Ireland</b> than reducing social media use.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The finding highlights the importance of <b>peer support, teacher relationships and school connectedness</b> for adolescent wellbeing.<br>• The report also examines <b>adolescent mental health, social media use and family support</b> across countries.<br>• <b>Social support</b> is one of the six key explanatory variables used in the World Happiness Report, along with GDP per capita and healthy life expectancy.<br>• Policies suggested include <b>school mental health programmes, reducing academic pressure and strengthening community bonds</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विद्यालय से अधिक जुड़ाव</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026</b> में पाया गया कि <b>विद्यालय से जुड़ाव</b> की भावना <b>यूनाइटेड किंगडम तथा आयरलैंड</b> की लड़कियों में सोशल मीडिया का उपयोग घटाने की तुलना में <b>जीवन संतुष्टि में अधिक सुधार</b> से जुड़ी थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह निष्कर्ष किशोर कल्याण के लिए <b>साथियों का सहयोग, शिक्षक संबंध तथा विद्यालय से जुड़ाव</b> के महत्व को रेखांकित करता है।<br>• रिपोर्ट में विभिन्न देशों में <b>किशोर मानसिक स्वास्थ्य, सोशल मीडिया उपयोग तथा पारिवारिक सहयोग</b> का भी विश्लेषण किया गया है।<br>• <b>सामाजिक सहायता</b> विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट में प्रयुक्त छह प्रमुख व्याख्यात्मक चरों में से एक है, साथ में प्रति व्यक्ति जीडीपी तथा स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा भी हैं।<br>• सुझाई गई नीतियों में <b>विद्यालय मानसिक स्वास्थ्य कार्यक्रम, शैक्षणिक दबाव कम करना तथा सामुदायिक संबंध मजबूत करना</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070229","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which statement best distinguishes abiotic components from biotic components in an ecosystem? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन किसी पारितंत्र में अजैविक घटकों को जैविक घटकों से सर्वोत्तम रूप से अलग करता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Soil bacteria are abiotic because they are microscopic.","hi":"मृदा जीवाणु अजैविक हैं क्योंकि वे सूक्ष्मदर्शी हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Organic compounds belong exclusively to biotic components.","hi":"कार्बनिक यौगिक केवल जैविक घटकों के होते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Temperature and topography affect species distribution.","hi":"तापमान तथा स्थलाकृति प्रजाति वितरण को प्रभावित करते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Producers are abiotic because they convert solar energy.","hi":"उत्पादक अजैविक हैं क्योंकि वे सौर ऊर्जा का रूपांतरण करते हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Temperature and topography affect species distribution.</b><br><b>Abiotic components</b> are the non-living physical and chemical factors of an ecosystem, such as <b>temperature, light, water, soil and topography</b>, which shape the distribution of living organisms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Biotic components</b> include <b>producers, consumers and decomposers</b>, while abiotic components include climatic, edaphic and topographic factors.<br>• <b>Soil bacteria</b> are living and therefore <b>biotic</b>, even though they are microscopic.<br>• <b>Organic compounds</b> such as humus and dead organic matter form part of the <b>abiotic</b> environment, so the second statement is wrong.<br>• <b>Producers</b> are living organisms that convert solar energy through photosynthesis, so they are <b>biotic</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – तापमान तथा स्थलाकृति प्रजाति वितरण को प्रभावित करते हैं।</b><br><b>अजैविक घटक</b> पारितंत्र के निर्जीव भौतिक एवं रासायनिक कारक हैं, जैसे <b>तापमान, प्रकाश, जल, मृदा तथा स्थलाकृति</b>, जो सजीवों के वितरण को आकार देते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जैविक घटकों</b> में <b>उत्पादक, उपभोक्ता तथा विघटनकर्ता</b> आते हैं, जबकि अजैविक घटकों में जलवायविक, मृदा संबंधी तथा स्थलाकृतिक कारक शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>मृदा जीवाणु</b> सजीव हैं, अतः <b>जैविक</b> हैं, चाहे वे सूक्ष्मदर्शी हों।<br>• <b>कार्बनिक यौगिक</b> जैसे ह्यूमस तथा मृत कार्बनिक पदार्थ <b>अजैविक</b> पर्यावरण का भाग हैं, अतः दूसरा कथन गलत है।<br>• <b>उत्पादक</b> सजीव हैं जो प्रकाश संश्लेषण से सौर ऊर्जा का रूपांतरण करते हैं, अतः वे <b>जैविक</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070230","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"A wetland ecosystem is invaded by aquatic weeds after nutrient enrichment from fertilizers. Which sequence correctly describes the ecological process? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उर्वरकों से पोषक तत्वों के संवर्धन के बाद किसी आर्द्रभूमि पारितंत्र पर जलीय खरपतवार का आक्रमण हो जाता है। कौन-सा क्रम पारिस्थितिक प्रक्रिया का सही वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Oxygen enrichment, fish proliferation, reduced decomposition, algal decline","hi":"ऑक्सीजन संवर्धन, मत्स्य वृद्धि, घटता विघटन, शैवाल में कमी"},"2":{"en":"Nutrient loading, eutrophication, oxygen depletion, aquatic mortality","hi":"पोषक भारण, यूट्रोफिकेशन, ऑक्सीजन की कमी, जलीय जीवों की मृत्यु"},"3":{"en":"Weed invasion, salinity increase, coral bleaching, reef degradation","hi":"खरपतवार आक्रमण, लवणता में वृद्धि, प्रवाल विरंजन, प्रवाल भित्ति का क्षरण"},"4":{"en":"Nutrient reduction, increased decomposition, oxygen depletion, fish extinction","hi":"पोषक तत्वों में कमी, बढ़ता विघटन, ऑक्सीजन की कमी, मछलियों का विलोपन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Nutrient loading, eutrophication, oxygen depletion, aquatic mortality</b><br>Fertilizer runoff causes <b>nutrient loading</b> (mainly nitrogen and phosphorus), leading to <b>eutrophication</b>, excessive algal growth, <b>oxygen depletion</b> as algae decompose, and finally <b>mortality of aquatic organisms</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Eutrophication</b> is the enrichment of water bodies with nutrients, causing <b>algal blooms</b> and <b>weed growth</b>.<br>• When algae die, bacteria decompose them and consume <b>dissolved oxygen</b>, creating <b>hypoxic or anoxic</b> conditions that kill fish.<br>• The process also increases <b>turbidity, reduces light penetration and causes foul odour</b> in the water body.<br>• Control measures include <b>reducing fertilizer runoff, treating sewage, using buffer strips and harvesting aquatic weeds</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पोषक भारण, यूट्रोफिकेशन, ऑक्सीजन की कमी, जलीय जीवों की मृत्यु</b><br>उर्वरकों का बहाव <b>पोषक भारण</b> (मुख्यतः नाइट्रोजन एवं फॉस्फोरस) करता है, जिससे <b>यूट्रोफिकेशन</b>, अत्यधिक शैवाल वृद्धि, शैवाल के विघटन से <b>ऑक्सीजन की कमी</b> तथा अंततः <b>जलीय जीवों की मृत्यु</b> होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>यूट्रोफिकेशन</b> जल निकायों में पोषक तत्वों का संवर्धन है, जिससे <b>शैवाल प्रस्फुटन</b> तथा <b>खरपतवार वृद्धि</b> होती है।<br>• शैवाल के मरने पर जीवाणु उनका विघटन करते हैं और <b>घुलित ऑक्सीजन</b> खर्च करते हैं, जिससे <b>अल्पऑक्सीजन अथवा अनॉक्सी</b> स्थिति बनती है और मछलियाँ मर जाती हैं।<br>• इस प्रक्रिया से जल में <b>गंदलापन बढ़ता है, प्रकाश का प्रवेश घटता है तथा दुर्गंध</b> उत्पन्न होती है।<br>• नियंत्रण के उपायों में <b>उर्वरक बहाव कम करना, मलजल शोधन, बफर पट्टियाँ तथा जलीय खरपतवार निकालना</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070231","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If a nine-digit number 489x6378y is divisible by 72, then the value of \\(\\sqrt{8x + 6y}\\) will be: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि नौ अंकों की संख्या 489x6378y, 72 से विभाज्य है, तो \\(\\sqrt{8x + 6y}\\) का मान होगा: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"72 = 8 × 9<br>Divisible by 8: the last three digits 78y must be divisible by 8, and \\(784 = 8 \\times 98\\), so \\(y = 4\\)<br>Divisible by 9: digit sum \\(= 4+8+9+x+6+3+7+8+4 = 49 + x\\) must be a multiple of 9, so \\(x = 5\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{8x + 6y} = \\sqrt{40 + 24} = \\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8.</b>","hi":"72 = 8 × 9<br>8 से विभाज्यता: अंतिम तीन अंक 78y, 8 से विभाज्य होने चाहिए और \\(784 = 8 \\times 98\\), अतः \\(y = 4\\)<br>9 से विभाज्यता: अंकों का योग \\(= 4+8+9+x+6+3+7+8+4 = 49 + x\\), 9 का गुणज होना चाहिए, अतः \\(x = 5\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{8x + 6y} = \\sqrt{40 + 24} = \\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070232","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Convert 3π radians to degrees. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3π रेडियन को डिग्री में बदलिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"540°"},"2":{"en":"50°"},"3":{"en":"510°"},"4":{"en":"70°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(3\\pi \\text{ radians} = 3\\pi \\times \\frac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 180^\\circ = \\boxed{540^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 540°.</b>","hi":"\\(3\\pi \\text{ रेडियन} = 3\\pi \\times \\frac{180^\\circ}{\\pi}\\)<br>\\(= 3 \\times 180^\\circ = \\boxed{540^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 540° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070233","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tanθ + cotθ = 2, then what is the value of tan²θ + cot²θ? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि tanθ + cotθ = 2 है, तो tan²θ + cot²θ का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan^2\\theta + \\cot^2\\theta = (\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta)^2 - 2\\tan\\theta\\cot\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 2^2 - 2(1)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan^2\\theta + \\cot^2\\theta = (\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta)^2 - 2\\tan\\theta\\cot\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 2^2 - 2(1)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070234","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The total surface area of a cone is 616 cm², and its radius is 7 cm. Find the height of the cone. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंकु का कुल पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 616 cm² है और इसकी त्रिज्या 7 cm है। शंकु की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 cm"},"2":{"en":"19.8 cm"},"3":{"en":"20.50 cm"},"4":{"en":"24.6 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 30L65 130M120 30L175 130\"/><path d=\"M65 130a55 14 0 0 0 110 0\"/><path d=\"M65 130a55 14 0 0 1 110 0\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 30V130\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 130H175\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"130\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">7</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">7</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">l = 21</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">l = 21</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r(l + r) = 616\\)<br>\\(\\frac{22}{7} \\times 7(l + 7) = 616 \\Rightarrow l + 7 = 28 \\Rightarrow l = 21\\)<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{l^2 - r^2} = \\sqrt{441 - 49} = \\sqrt{392}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{19.8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 19.8 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 30L65 130M120 30L175 130\"/><path d=\"M65 130a55 14 0 0 0 110 0\"/><path d=\"M65 130a55 14 0 0 1 110 0\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 30V130\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 130H175\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"30\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"130\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">7</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">7</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">l = 21</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">l = 21</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r(l + r) = 616\\)<br>\\(\\frac{22}{7} \\times 7(l + 7) = 616 \\Rightarrow l + 7 = 28 \\Rightarrow l = 21\\)<br>\\(h = \\sqrt{l^2 - r^2} = \\sqrt{441 - 49} = \\sqrt{392}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{19.8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 19.8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070235","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"If a: b: c = 3: 4: 5 and a + 2b + c = 48, find the value of c. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a: b: c = 3: 4: 5 और a + 2b + c = 48 है, तो c का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let a = 3k, b = 4k, c = 5k<br>\\(3k + 8k + 5k = 48 \\Rightarrow 16k = 48 \\Rightarrow k = 3\\)<br>\\(c = 5k = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 15.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए a = 3k, b = 4k, c = 5k<br>\\(3k + 8k + 5k = 48 \\Rightarrow 16k = 48 \\Rightarrow k = 3\\)<br>\\(c = 5k = \\boxed{15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070236","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"Sixty per cent of Anil's monthly income is equal to seventy-five per cent of Sunil's monthly income. If Anil's income is reduced by ₹300 while Sunil's income remains unchanged, the ratio of their new incomes becomes 7: 6. Find Sunil's monthly income. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अनिल की मासिक आय का साठ प्रतिशत सुनील की मासिक आय के पचहत्तर प्रतिशत के बराबर है। यदि अनिल की आय ₹300 कम हो जाए जबकि सुनील की आय अपरिवर्तित रहे, तो उनकी नई आय का अनुपात 7: 6 हो जाता है। सुनील की मासिक आय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2900"},"2":{"en":"₹5000"},"3":{"en":"₹3600"},"4":{"en":"₹4200"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(0.60A = 0.75S \\Rightarrow A = 1.25S\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.25S - 300}{S} = \\frac{7}{6}\\)<br>\\(7.5S - 1800 = 7S \\Rightarrow 0.5S = 1800\\)<br>\\(S = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹3600.</b>","hi":"\\(0.60A = 0.75S \\Rightarrow A = 1.25S\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1.25S - 300}{S} = \\frac{7}{6}\\)<br>\\(7.5S - 1800 = 7S \\Rightarrow 0.5S = 1800\\)<br>\\(S = \\boxed{3600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹3600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070237","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"Determine the number of integers between 200 and 600 that are divisible by both 5 and 7. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"200 और 600 के बीच ऐसे पूर्णांकों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए जो 5 और 7 दोनों से विभाज्य हैं। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"11"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"13"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Numbers divisible by both 5 and 7 are multiples of LCM(5, 7) = 35<br>Multiples of 35 from 200 to 600: 210, 245, …, 595<br>Count = \\(\\frac{595}{35} - \\frac{210}{35} + 1 = 17 - 6 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12.</b>","hi":"5 और 7 दोनों से विभाज्य संख्याएँ LCM(5, 7) = 35 के गुणज हैं<br>200 से 600 तक 35 के गुणज: 210, 245, …, 595<br>संख्या = \\(\\frac{595}{35} - \\frac{210}{35} + 1 = 17 - 6 + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070238","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A certain sum of money amounts to ₹5,832 in 2 years at 8% per annum compound interest. Find the principal. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोई धनराशि 8% वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर 2 वर्षों में ₹5,832 हो जाती है। मूलधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹4000"},"2":{"en":"₹4700"},"3":{"en":"₹5000"},"4":{"en":"₹5500"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(5832 = P\\left(1 + \\frac{8}{100}\\right)^2 = P(1.08)^2\\)<br>\\(5832 = 1.1664P\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{5832}{1.1664} = \\boxed{5000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹5000.</b>","hi":"\\(5832 = P\\left(1 + \\frac{8}{100}\\right)^2 = P(1.08)^2\\)<br>\\(5832 = 1.1664P\\)<br>\\(P = \\frac{5832}{1.1664} = \\boxed{5000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹5000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070239","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A tower of height 210 m observes two points on the same line at angles of depression 30° and 60°. Find the approximate distance between the points.(Use √3=1.732) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"210 m ऊँची एक मीनार से उसी रेखा पर स्थित दो बिंदुओं के अवनमन कोण 30° और 60° हैं। उन बिंदुओं के बीच की अनुमानित दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए।(√3=1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"248 m"},"2":{"en":"252 m"},"3":{"en":"242 m"},"4":{"en":"239 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"300\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M14 152H282\"/><path d=\"M30 152V20H40V152\"/><path d=\"M30 20H62\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M30 20L105 152M30 20L263 152\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">210</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">210</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">60°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">60°</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">≈ 242 m</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">≈ 242 m</text></g></svg><br>Far point: \\(AD = \\frac{210}{\\tan 30^\\circ} = 210\\sqrt{3} = 363.72\\) m<br>Near point: \\(AC = \\frac{210}{\\tan 60^\\circ} = \\frac{210}{\\sqrt{3}} = 121.24\\) m<br>Distance = \\(363.72 - 121.24 = 242.48 \\approx \\boxed{242}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 242 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"300\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M14 152H282\"/><path d=\"M30 152V20H40V152\"/><path d=\"M30 20H62\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M30 20L105 152M30 20L263 152\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">210</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">210</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">60°</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">60°</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"263\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">≈ 242 m</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">≈ 242 m</text></g></svg><br>दूर बिंदु: \\(AD = \\frac{210}{\\tan 30^\\circ} = 210\\sqrt{3} = 363.72\\) m<br>निकट बिंदु: \\(AC = \\frac{210}{\\tan 60^\\circ} = \\frac{210}{\\sqrt{3}} = 121.24\\) m<br>दूरी = \\(363.72 - 121.24 = 242.48 \\approx \\boxed{242}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 242 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070240","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A rhombus has a perimeter of 52 cm, and one of its diagonals measures 10 cm. Calculate the area of the rhombus. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक समचतुर्भुज का परिमाप 52 cm है और इसका एक विकर्ण 10 cm है। समचतुर्भुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120 cm²"},"2":{"en":"130 cm²"},"3":{"en":"240 cm²"},"4":{"en":"260 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 170\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M49 95L145 55L241 95L145 135Z\"/><path d=\"M49 95H241M145 55V135\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M145 87H151M149 95V103\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"95\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">13 cm</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">13 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">24 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">24 cm</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10 cm</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10 cm</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text></g></svg><br>Side = \\(\\frac{52}{4} = 13\\) cm, half of the given diagonal = 5 cm<br>Other half diagonal = \\(\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = 12\\) cm \\(\\Rightarrow\\) second diagonal = 24 cm<br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} d_1 d_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 24 = \\boxed{120}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 120 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 170\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M49 95L145 55L241 95L145 135Z\"/><path d=\"M49 95H241M145 55V135\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M145 87H151M149 95V103\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"95\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">13 cm</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"66\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">13 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">24 cm</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">24 cm</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10 cm</text><text x=\"152\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10 cm</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"246\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text></g></svg><br>भुजा = \\(\\frac{52}{4} = 13\\) cm, दिए गए विकर्ण का आधा = 5 cm<br>दूसरे विकर्ण का आधा = \\(\\sqrt{13^2 - 5^2} = 12\\) cm \\(\\Rightarrow\\) दूसरा विकर्ण = 24 cm<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} d_1 d_2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 24 = \\boxed{120}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 120 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070241","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}}\\). [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}} = \\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}\\) because \\((\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}\\)<br>Expression = \\((\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) - (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}} = \\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}\\) क्योंकि \\((\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\((\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}) - (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070242","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}}}\\). [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{8}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{8}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}} = \\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}\\) because \\((\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7})^2 = 15 - 2\\sqrt{56}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}} = \\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7}\\)<br>Expression = \\((\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}) - (\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{7}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{7}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{15 - 2\\sqrt{56}} = \\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}\\) क्योंकि \\((\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7})^2 = 15 - 2\\sqrt{56}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}} = \\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7}\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\((\\sqrt{8} - \\sqrt{7}) - (\\sqrt{8} + \\sqrt{7})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{7}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{7}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070243","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hemisphere is carved out of a wooden block of side 14 cm. What is the maximum possible surface area of the resulting solid? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"14 cm भुजा वाले एक लकड़ी के गुटके से एक अर्धगोला काटा जाता है। परिणामी ठोस का अधिकतम संभव पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1176 cm²"},"2":{"en":"1330 cm²"},"3":{"en":"1078 cm²"},"4":{"en":"1232 cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"220\" height=\"195\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 195\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 60H150V160H50Z\"/><path d=\"M64 46H164V146H64Z\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M50 60L64 46M150 60L164 46M150 160L164 146\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100a17.2 17.2 0 1 0 34.4 0a17.2 17.2 0 1 0 -34.4 0\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100A17.2 9 0 0 1 143.2 100\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100A17.2 9 0 0 0 143.2 100\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">14 cm</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">14 cm</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 7</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 7</text></g></svg><br>Largest hemisphere has radius = 7 cm<br>Surface area = cube surface − circle + curved surface of hemisphere<br>\\(= 6 \\times 14^2 - \\pi r^2 + 2\\pi r^2 = 1176 + \\pi r^2\\)<br>\\(= 1176 + \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 1176 + 154\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1330}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1330 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"220\" height=\"195\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 195\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 60H150V160H50Z\"/><path d=\"M64 46H164V146H64Z\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M50 60L64 46M150 60L164 46M150 160L164 146\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100a17.2 17.2 0 1 0 34.4 0a17.2 17.2 0 1 0 -34.4 0\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100A17.2 9 0 0 1 143.2 100\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M108.8 100A17.2 9 0 0 0 143.2 100\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">14 cm</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">14 cm</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 7</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 7</text></g></svg><br>सबसे बड़े अर्धगोले की त्रिज्या = 7 cm<br>पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = घन का पृष्ठ − वृत्त + अर्धगोले का वक्र पृष्ठ<br>\\(= 6 \\times 14^2 - \\pi r^2 + 2\\pi r^2 = 1176 + \\pi r^2\\)<br>\\(= 1176 + \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 1176 + 154\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1330}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1330 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070244","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of length 12 cm is at a distance of 8 cm from the center of a circle. What is the radius of the circle? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"12 cm लंबाई की एक जीवा वृत्त के केंद्र से 8 cm की दूरी पर है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"8 cm"},"3":{"en":"10 cm"},"4":{"en":"12 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"195\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 195\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"70\"/><path d=\"M78 156H162\"/><path d=\"M120 100V156\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 100L162 156\"/><path d=\"M120 148H128V156\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10</text></g></svg><br>Half chord = \\(\\frac{12}{2} = 6\\) cm<br>Radius = \\(\\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 36}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"195\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 195\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"70\"/><path d=\"M78 156H162\"/><path d=\"M120 100V156\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 100L162 156\"/><path d=\"M120 148H128V156\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10</text></g></svg><br>जीवा का आधा = \\(\\frac{12}{2} = 6\\) cm<br>त्रिज्या = \\(\\sqrt{8^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 36}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070245","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"Let f : Q → Q be a field automorphism. How many such automorphisms exist? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान लीजिए f : Q → Q एक क्षेत्र स्वाकारित्व (field automorphism) है। ऐसे कितने स्वाकारित्व होते हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Uncountably many","hi":"अगणनीय रूप से अनेक"},"2":{"en":"Exactly 2 (identity and negation)","hi":"ठीक 2 (तत्समक और ऋणात्मक)"},"3":{"en":"Exactly 1 (the identity)","hi":"ठीक 1 (तत्समक)"},"4":{"en":"Countably infinitely many","hi":"गणनीय रूप से अनंत"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Any automorphism of Q fixes 1, hence fixes every integer<br>It also fixes every fraction, since \\(f\\left(\\frac{m}{n}\\right) = \\frac{f(m)}{f(n)} = \\frac{m}{n}\\)<br>So every element of Q is fixed<br>Only the identity map works: \\(\\boxed{\\text{Exactly 1 (the identity)}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Exactly 1 (the identity).</b>","hi":"Q का कोई भी स्वाकारित्व 1 को स्थिर रखता है, अतः हर पूर्णांक को स्थिर रखता है<br>यह हर भिन्न को भी स्थिर रखता है, क्योंकि \\(f\\left(\\frac{m}{n}\\right) = \\frac{f(m)}{f(n)} = \\frac{m}{n}\\)<br>इसलिए Q का प्रत्येक अवयव स्थिर है<br>केवल तत्समक प्रतिचित्रण संभव है: \\(\\boxed{\\text{ठीक 1 (तत्समक)}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ठीक 1 (तत्समक) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070246","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"What is the difference between the squares of the consecutive numbers 51 and 50? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"क्रमागत संख्याओं 51 और 50 के वर्गों के बीच का अंतर क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"99"},"2":{"en":"100"},"3":{"en":"101"},"4":{"en":"111"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(51^2 - 50^2 = (51 + 50)(51 - 50)\\)<br>\\(= 101 \\times 1 = \\boxed{101}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 101.</b>","hi":"\\(51^2 - 50^2 = (51 + 50)(51 - 50)\\)<br>\\(= 101 \\times 1 = \\boxed{101}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 101 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070247","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A textile trader borrowed ₹1,25,000 and agreed to repay the loan under simple interest terms. After 4 years, he repaid ₹1,65,000. If he had borrowed ₹2,00,000 at the same rate for 7 years, calculate the amount he would have repaid. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वस्त्र व्यापारी ने ₹1,25,000 उधार लिए और साधारण ब्याज की शर्तों पर ऋण चुकाने का वचन दिया। 4 वर्षों के बाद उसने ₹1,65,000 चुकाए। यदि उसने उसी दर पर 7 वर्षों के लिए ₹2,00,000 उधार लिए होते, तो वह कितनी राशि चुकाता, इसकी गणना कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3,12,000"},"2":{"en":"₹3,55,000"},"3":{"en":"₹3,88,000"},"4":{"en":"₹3,19,000"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Interest for 4 years = \\(165000 - 125000 = 40000\\)<br>\\(40000 = \\frac{125000 \\times 4 \\times r}{100} \\Rightarrow r = 8\\)%<br>Interest on ₹2,00,000 for 7 years = \\(\\frac{200000 \\times 8 \\times 7}{100} = 112000\\)<br>Amount = \\(200000 + 112000 = \\boxed{312000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹3,12,000.</b>","hi":"4 वर्ष का ब्याज = \\(165000 - 125000 = 40000\\)<br>\\(40000 = \\frac{125000 \\times 4 \\times r}{100} \\Rightarrow r = 8\\)%<br>₹2,00,000 पर 7 वर्ष का ब्याज = \\(\\frac{200000 \\times 8 \\times 7}{100} = 112000\\)<br>मिश्रधन = \\(200000 + 112000 = \\boxed{312000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹3,12,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070248","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(sec^2X + cosec^2X = 4\\), what is the value of sinX cosX? (Assume X is an acute angle.) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(sec^2X + cosec^2X = 4\\) है, तो sinX cosX का मान क्या है? (मान लीजिए X न्यून कोण है।) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 X} + \\frac{1}{\\sin^2 X} = \\frac{\\sin^2 X + \\cos^2 X}{\\sin^2 X\\cos^2 X} = 4\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 X\\cos^2 X = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\sin X\\cos X = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 X} + \\frac{1}{\\sin^2 X} = \\frac{\\sin^2 X + \\cos^2 X}{\\sin^2 X\\cos^2 X} = 4\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 X\\cos^2 X = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(\\sin X\\cos X = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070249","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Mechanics X, Y and Z can assemble an engine alone in 15 days, 20 days and 30 days, respectively. A floor supervisor D does no physical assembling. However, due to her expertise, X's efficiency increases by 20%, that of Y increases by 25 % and that of Z increases by 50%, whenever D supervises them individually. D can supervise only one person at a time, but all the three mechanics work simultaneously from start to end. Find out who should D supervise so that the assembling gets completed in the absolute minimum number of days and find the time required in that case, respectively. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मिस्त्री X, Y और Z अकेले एक इंजन को क्रमशः 15 दिन, 20 दिन और 30 दिन में जोड़ सकते हैं। फ्लोर सुपरवाइज़र D स्वयं कोई शारीरिक कार्य नहीं करती। लेकिन अपनी विशेषज्ञता के कारण, जब भी D उन्हें व्यक्तिगत रूप से पर्यवेक्षण करती है, X की कार्यक्षमता 20%, Y की 25% और Z की 50% बढ़ जाती है। D एक समय में केवल एक व्यक्ति का पर्यवेक्षण कर सकती है, लेकिन तीनों मिस्त्री शुरू से अंत तक एक साथ कार्य करते हैं। ज्ञात कीजिए कि न्यूनतम दिनों में जोड़ने का कार्य पूरा होने के लिए D को किसका पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए और उस स्थिति में आवश्यक समय क्रमशः कितना है। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D should supervise X; 5 days","hi":"D को X का पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए; 5 दिन"},"2":{"en":"D should supervise Y; 6 days","hi":"D को Y का पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए; 6 दिन"},"3":{"en":"D should supervise Z; 6 days","hi":"D को Z का पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए; 6 दिन"},"4":{"en":"D can supervise any of the three; 4 days","hi":"D तीनों में से किसी का भी पर्यवेक्षण कर सकती है; 4 दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Work = 60 units \\(\\Rightarrow\\) X = 4, Y = 3, Z = 2 units/day<br>Supervised rates: X = \\(4 \\times 1.2 = 4.8\\), Y = \\(3 \\times 1.25 = 3.75\\), Z = \\(2 \\times 1.5 = 3\\)<br>Supervise X: \\(4.8 + 3 + 2 = 9.8\\) \\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{60}{9.8} = 6.12\\) days<br>Supervise Y: \\(4 + 3.75 + 2 = 9.75\\) \\(\\Rightarrow 6.15\\) days<br>Supervise Z: \\(4 + 3 + 3 = 10\\) \\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{60}{10} = 6\\) days<br>Minimum = \\(\\boxed{\\text{D should supervise Z; 6 days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): D should supervise Z; 6 days.</b>","hi":"कार्य = 60 इकाई \\(\\Rightarrow\\) X = 4, Y = 3, Z = 2 इकाई/दिन<br>पर्यवेक्षण के साथ दरें: X = \\(4 \\times 1.2 = 4.8\\), Y = \\(3 \\times 1.25 = 3.75\\), Z = \\(2 \\times 1.5 = 3\\)<br>X का पर्यवेक्षण: \\(4.8 + 3 + 2 = 9.8\\) \\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{60}{9.8} = 6.12\\) दिन<br>Y का पर्यवेक्षण: \\(4 + 3.75 + 2 = 9.75\\) \\(\\Rightarrow 6.15\\) दिन<br>Z का पर्यवेक्षण: \\(4 + 3 + 3 = 10\\) \\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{60}{10} = 6\\) दिन<br>न्यूनतम = \\(\\boxed{\\text{D को Z का पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए; 6 दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): D को Z का पर्यवेक्षण करना चाहिए; 6 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070250","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If the radii of two circles are in the ratio 2:3 and arcs of equal length on them subtend angles \\(\\theta_1\\) and \\(\\theta_2\\) at their centers, find \\(\\frac{\\theta_1}{\\theta_2}\\). [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि दो वृत्तों की त्रिज्याएँ 2:3 के अनुपात में हैं और उन पर समान लंबाई के चाप उनके केंद्रों पर \\(\\theta_1\\) और \\(\\theta_2\\) कोण अंतरित करते हैं, तो \\(\\frac{\\theta_1}{\\theta_2}\\) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{9}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Arc length = \\(r\\theta\\), and both arcs are equal<br>\\(2\\theta_1 = 3\\theta_2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\theta_1}{\\theta_2} = \\frac{3}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"चाप की लंबाई = \\(r\\theta\\), और दोनों चाप बराबर हैं<br>\\(2\\theta_1 = 3\\theta_2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{\\theta_1}{\\theta_2} = \\frac{3}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070251","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If A + B = 90°, what is tan A · tan B equal to? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि A + B = 90° है, तो tan A · tan B किसके बराबर है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"cot²A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(B = 90^\\circ - A \\Rightarrow \\tan B = \\cot A\\)<br>\\(\\tan A \\cdot \\tan B = \\tan A \\cdot \\cot A = 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(B = 90^\\circ - A \\Rightarrow \\tan B = \\cot A\\)<br>\\(\\tan A \\cdot \\tan B = \\tan A \\cdot \\cot A = 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070252","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 62\\), what is the positive value of \\(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\)? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 62\\) है, तो \\(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\) का धनात्मक मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} + 2\\)<br>\\(= 62 + 2 = 64\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8.</b>","hi":"\\(\\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} + 2\\)<br>\\(= 62 + 2 = 64\\)<br>\\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070253","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A circle is inscribed in a quadrilateral ABCD touching all its sides. If the line segments joining the center O to the vertices A and B form ΔAOB, and the consecutive angles satisfy (∠C + ∠D = 180°) (a trapezium configuration), what is the measure of ∠AOB? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त चतुर्भुज ABCD में अंतर्निहित है जो इसकी सभी भुजाओं को स्पर्श करता है। यदि केंद्र O को शीर्षों A और B से जोड़ने वाले रेखाखंड ΔAOB बनाते हैं, और क्रमागत कोण (∠C + ∠D = 180°) को संतुष्ट करते हैं (एक समलंब संरचना), तो ∠AOB का माप क्या है? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45°"},"2":{"en":"60°"},"3":{"en":"90°"},"4":{"en":"120°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M45.7 40.5H194.3L156.4 144.5H83.6Z\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"92.5\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M120 92.5L45.7 40.5M120 92.5L83.6 144.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"92.5\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">90°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">90°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle C + \\angle D = 180^\\circ \\Rightarrow AD \\parallel BC\\)<br>The circle touches all four sides, so \\(\\angle A + \\angle B = 180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(OA\\) and \\(OB\\) bisect \\(\\angle A\\) and \\(\\angle B\\)<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 180^\\circ - \\frac{180^\\circ}{2} = \\boxed{90^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 90°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M45.7 40.5H194.3L156.4 144.5H83.6Z\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"92.5\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M120 92.5L45.7 40.5M120 92.5L83.6 144.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"92.5\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">90°</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">90°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle C + \\angle D = 180^\\circ \\Rightarrow AD \\parallel BC\\)<br>वृत्त चारों भुजाओं को स्पर्श करता है, अतः \\(\\angle A + \\angle B = 180^\\circ\\)<br>\\(OA\\) और \\(OB\\) क्रमशः \\(\\angle A\\) और \\(\\angle B\\) के समद्विभाजक हैं<br>\\(\\angle AOB = 180^\\circ - \\frac{180^\\circ}{2} = \\boxed{90^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 90° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070254","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, AB = AC = 10 units and BC = 12 units. A line is drawn through the centroid G parallel to BC, meeting AB at P and AC at Q. Find the length of PQ. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ΔABC में, AB = AC = 10 इकाई और BC = 12 इकाई है। केंद्रक G से होकर BC के समांतर एक रेखा खींची जाती है, जो AB को P पर और AC को Q पर मिलती है। PQ की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 units","hi":"6 इकाई"},"2":{"en":"7 units","hi":"7 इकाई"},"3":{"en":"8 units","hi":"8 इकाई"},"4":{"en":"9 units","hi":"9 इकाई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 70L60 150H180Z\"/><path d=\"M120 70V150\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M80 123.3H160\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"123.3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">G</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">G</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">12</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">12</text></g></svg><br>The centroid divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1 from the vertex<br>A line through the centroid parallel to BC cuts AB and AC at two-thirds of the height<br>\\(PQ = \\frac{2}{3} \\times BC = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 12 = \\boxed{8}\\) units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8 units.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M120 70L60 150H180Z\"/><path d=\"M120 70V150\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M80 123.3H160\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"123.3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">G</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">G</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">12</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">12</text></g></svg><br>केंद्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को शीर्ष से 2 : 1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है<br>केंद्रक से BC के समांतर खींची गई रेखा ऊँचाई के दो-तिहाई भाग पर AB और AC को काटती है<br>\\(PQ = \\frac{2}{3} \\times BC = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 12 = \\boxed{8}\\) इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070255","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two coplanar circles with radii 2 cm and 5 cm have their centers 11 cm apart. How many common tangents can be drawn to these circles? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"2 cm और 5 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो समतलीय वृत्तों के केंद्र 11 cm दूर हैं। इन वृत्तों पर कितनी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"310\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 310 205\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"108\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"108\" r=\"70\"/><path d=\"M64.2 86.4L195.7 54\"/><path d=\"M64.2 129.6L195.7 162\"/><path d=\"M101.6 84.7L220.3 169.2\"/><path d=\"M101.6 131.3L220.3 46.8\"/><path d=\"M82 108H240\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"108\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"108\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 2</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 2</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 5</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 5</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">11</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">11</text></g></svg><br>Sum of radii = \\(2 + 5 = 7\\) cm, which is less than the distance between centres = 11 cm<br>The circles are completely separate from each other<br>Such circles have 2 direct and 2 transverse common tangents<br>Total = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"310\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 310 205\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"108\" r=\"28\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"108\" r=\"70\"/><path d=\"M64.2 86.4L195.7 54\"/><path d=\"M64.2 129.6L195.7 162\"/><path d=\"M101.6 84.7L220.3 169.2\"/><path d=\"M101.6 131.3L220.3 46.8\"/><path d=\"M82 108H240\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"108\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"108\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 2</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 2</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 5</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 5</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">11</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">11</text></g></svg><br>त्रिज्याओं का योग = \\(2 + 5 = 7\\) cm, जो केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी 11 cm से कम है<br>वृत्त एक-दूसरे से पूर्णतः अलग हैं<br>ऐसे वृत्तों की 2 सीधी और 2 तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ होती हैं<br>कुल = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitution for the italicized phrase:<br>“After a long day, Maya sat by the window in <b>a state of being pleasantly lost in her thoughts</b>.” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Euphoria"},"2":{"en":"Solitude"},"3":{"en":"Reverie"},"4":{"en":"Delirium"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Reverie (स्वप्निल ध्यान) = pleasant absorption in dreamy thoughts.</b><br><b>Euphoria (अति-हर्ष)</b> = intense happiness<br><b>Solitude (एकांत)</b> = the state of being alone<br><b>Delirium (प्रलाप)</b> = confused, disturbed mental state<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Reverie.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the below given active voice sentence into passive voice.<br>“They celebrate Independence Day with great enthusiasm.” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Independence Day was celebrated with great enthusiasm by them"},"2":{"en":"Independence Day has been celebrated with great enthusiasm by them"},"3":{"en":"Independence Day is being celebrated with great enthusiasm by them"},"4":{"en":"Independence Day is celebrated with great enthusiasm by them"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple present passive = am/is/are + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “Independence Day” becomes the subject.<br>“Celebrate” becomes “is celebrated,” and “by them” expresses the agent.<br>The other options change the tense or aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Independence Day is celebrated with great enthusiasm by them.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br>She said that she had been living in Mumbai for three years. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said, “I live in Mumbai for three years”."},"2":{"en":"She said, “I had lived in Mumbai for three years”."},"3":{"en":"She said, “I have been living in Mumbai for three years”."},"4":{"en":"She said, “I will be living in Mumbai for three years”."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect continuous reverses to present perfect continuous.</b><br>“Had been living” becomes “have been living.”<br>The reported “she” returns to “I.”<br>The other options use incompatible tenses.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She said, “I have been living in Mumbai for three years”..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which spelling correctly refers to “a skilled legal professional”? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Attourney"},"2":{"en":"Attorney"},"3":{"en":"Atourney"},"4":{"en":"Attorny"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Attorney (वकील) = a legally qualified professional.</b><br>The correct spelling is “attorney.”<br><b>Attourney</b> adds “u”; <b>atourney</b> omits “t.”<br><b>Attorny</b> omits “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Attorney.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) in digital transactions<br>B) through UPI platforms<br>C) there has been exponential growth<br>D) in the last five years [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B-D-A-C"},"2":{"en":"A-C-D-B"},"3":{"en":"C-A-B-D"},"4":{"en":"D-B-C-A"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-A-B-D</b><br>C supplies the main clause: there has been exponential growth.<br>A identifies the area of growth, and B specifies the platforms.<br>D supplies the time frame: the last five years.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C-A-B-D.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Turn the page” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Publish a new chapter"},"2":{"en":"Forget the past and start anew"},"3":{"en":"Add suspense to a story"},"4":{"en":"Reveal a plot twist"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Turn the page (नई शुरुआत करना) = move on from the past.</b><br>Example: “It is time to turn the page and rebuild our lives.”<br>Publishing, suspense and plot twists are unrelated.<br>The idiom expresses a fresh beginning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Forget the past and start anew.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Skeleton in the closet” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A hidden treasure"},"2":{"en":"An unknown character in a book"},"3":{"en":"A family heirloom"},"4":{"en":"A hidden shame or scandal"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>A skeleton in the closet (छिपा हुआ कलंक) = a discreditable secret.</b><br>Example: “Every family has a skeleton in the closet.”<br>Treasure, fictional characters and heirlooms are not implied.<br>The idiom concerns concealed shame.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): A hidden shame or scandal.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Bark is worse than bite” [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Looks better than it is"},"2":{"en":"Threat is worse than action"},"3":{"en":"Sound is louder"},"4":{"en":"Dog is angry"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Someone’s bark is worse than their bite = their threats are worse than their actions.</b><br>Example: “Don’t fear his shouting; his bark is worse than his bite.”<br>The idiom is figurative and does not simply concern dogs or sound.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Threat is worse than action.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>Despite of the warnings (1)/ he ventured into the forest (2)/ without any gear (3)/ or backup plan. (4) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Despite” is not followed by “of.”</b><br>Part (1) should read “<b>Despite</b> the warnings” or “<b>In spite of</b> the warnings.”<br>The preposition “of” is redundant.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The diplomat tried to brush off (1)/ the allegations but the press (2)/ kept pressing on (3)/ until he broke out. (4) [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Break down” means lose emotional control; “break out” means escape or begin suddenly.</b><br>Part (4) should read “until he <b>broke down</b>.”<br>The context requires an emotional collapse under pressure.<br>The other phrasal verbs are appropriate.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): (4).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The speaker's rhetoric was replete with appeals to emotion but lacked the ___ of empirical substantiation. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"depth"},"2":{"en":"rigor"},"3":{"en":"tone"},"4":{"en":"validity"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rigor (यथार्थता/कठोर परिश्रम) = strict precision and thoroughness.</b><br>Emotional rhetoric lacked the rigor of empirical support.<br>“Depth” is possible generally but does not express methodological exactness.<br>Tone and validity do not fit the possessive construction as precisely.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): rigor.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the appropriate one-word substitution for:<br>A person who cannot hear. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Blind"},"2":{"en":"Speechless"},"3":{"en":"Mute"},"4":{"en":"Deaf"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Deaf (बधिर) = unable to hear.</b><br><b>Blind (अंधा)</b> = unable to see<br><b>Speechless (मौन)</b> = temporarily unable or unwilling to speak<br><b>Mute (गूंगा)</b> = unable to speak<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Deaf.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of these is NOT a misspelt word? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Definately"},"2":{"en":"Definetely"},"3":{"en":"Definitely"},"4":{"en":"Definitly"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Definitely (निश्चित रूप से) = without doubt.</b><br>Only “definitely” is correctly spelled.<br><b>Definately</b> uses “a”; <b>definetely</b> inserts “e” after “n.”<br><b>Definitly</b> omits “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Definitely.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>Her actions were seen as <b>complementary</b> rather than conflicting. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"complimentary"},"2":{"en":"complementary"},"3":{"en":"complimented"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Complementary (पूरक) = combining well to complete or enhance something.</b><br>The sentence contrasts complementary actions with conflicting ones.<br>“Complimentary” means praising or free; “complimented” is a verb form.<br>The correctly keyed replacement remains “complementary.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): complementary.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence:<br><b>Not only the minister has denied</b> the allegations, but also filed a counter-suit. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"did the minister deny"},"2":{"en":"the minister has denied"},"3":{"en":"did the minister denied"},"4":{"en":"had the minister deny"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Negative introductory “not only” requires subject–auxiliary inversion.</b><br>“Not only did the minister deny …, but also filed …” uses the base verb after “did.”<br>B lacks inversion, C incorrectly uses past tense after “did.”<br>D uses an inappropriate past perfect structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): did the minister deny.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The panel will have finalized the report. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The report would be finalized by the panel."},"2":{"en":"The report has been finalized by the panel."},"3":{"en":"The report will have been finalized by the panel."},"4":{"en":"The report will be finalizing by the panel."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Future perfect passive = will have been + past participle.</b><br>The object “the report” becomes the subject.<br>“Will have finalized” becomes “will have been finalized.”<br>The other options change the tense or use an invalid passive form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The report will have been finalized by the panel..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The linguist noted that the prioritization of grammatical purity over communicative intent often marginalizes dialects that embody rich socio-cultural realities. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“When we prioritize grammar over meaning, we push out dialects that carry culture,” the linguist said."},"2":{"en":"“Focusing too much on grammar sidelines dialects full of cultural depth,” the linguist observed."},"3":{"en":"“Strict grammar norms marginalize dialects that carry sociocultural meaning,” she noted."},"4":{"en":"“Grammar obsession causes linguistic exclusion,” said the linguist."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Direct speech should preserve the complete causal relationship and sociocultural content.</b><br>A includes prioritizing grammar over meaning, marginalizing dialects, and their cultural role.<br>B and C condense parts of the idea, while D omits the dialects and cultural realities.<br>A most fully conveys the original statement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “When we prioritize grammar over meaning, we push out dialects that carry culture,” the linguist said..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P: in emerging democracies<br>Q: media literacy<br>R: must be integrated<br>S: into school curricula [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"QSRP"},"3":{"en":"RQPS"},"4":{"en":"RPQS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRSP</b><br>Q supplies the subject “media literacy,” and R the modal predicate “must be integrated.”<br>S states where it must be integrated.<br>P places the requirement in emerging democracies.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QRSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. after a decade of legal deliberations and forensic analysis<br>Q. was conclusively settled by the supreme adjudicating body<br>R. the dispute over land ownership<br>S. in favor of the indigenous claimants [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RQPS"},"2":{"en":"RPSQ"},"3":{"en":"QRSP"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQPS</b><br>R supplies the subject: the dispute over land ownership.<br>Q gives the main passive predicate.<br>P provides the preceding time and process, and S names the favoured party.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RQPS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. A barcode is scanned at the billing counter.<br>2. Items are bagged after successful payment.<br>3. The system generates an itemized receipt.<br>4. The customer proceeds to exit with the purchase. [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"3":{"en":"3-2-1-4"},"4":{"en":"1-2-3-4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-2-4</b><br>The barcode is scanned and the system generates an itemized receipt.<br>Items are bagged after successful payment.<br>The customer then exits with the purchase.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1-3-2-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In an era of saturation with new media, the dissemination of counterfeit information in the media has become an irreversible threat to social cohesion. Though disinformation in the past was at least contained by geography and language, fabricated fiction in the present sweeps around the world in a matter of seconds—presenting themselves as respectful journalism, falsified photos, or taken-out-of-context morsels of fact. The pervasiveness of social media has made fact-checking more of a reactive than a proactive role and generally permits distortions to become established before correction can occur.<br><br>The effects extend far beyond simple confusion. Manipulated media drive political action, fuel communal tensions, and erode trust in democratic institutions. If citizens cannot tell good sources of information from bad, democratic processes suffer, as public opinion is shaped by vetted facts rather than viral disinformation. In worst-case scenarios, disinformation has even prompted violence or destroyed health initiatives, as witnessed around the global pandemic.<br><br>Added to this problem is also the emergence of algorithm-fed aggregation of content, which further enriches echo chambers. The user is constantly given information that will most likely reinforce their current beliefs, creating a loop of feedback that legitimates falsity and bars dissonant truths. In the meantime, deepfakes and AI-generated content introduced an aspect of novelty in the crisis wherein fabrication is basically rendered indistinguishable from truth.<br><br>To combat this threat, however, calls for more than simply technical counter-response; it calls for media literacy, institutional disclosure, and a recasting of how truth is built and presented in a post-truth world. Without profound systemic change, the distinction between information and manipulation will always be blurry, threatening the very foundations of informed citizenship.<br><br><br>According to the passage, what has made fake media a uniquely modern threat? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"State-imposed censorship"},"2":{"en":"Restricted TV access"},"3":{"en":"Instant global digital diffusion"},"4":{"en":"Misuse of print journalism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Fabricated fiction now sweeps around the world in seconds.</b><br>Earlier disinformation was contained by geography and language.<br>Instant global digital diffusion therefore defines the uniquely modern threat.<br>The other options are not identified in the passage.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Instant global digital diffusion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In an era of saturation with new media, the dissemination of counterfeit information in the media has become an irreversible threat to social cohesion. Though disinformation in the past was at least contained by geography and language, fabricated fiction in the present sweeps around the world in a matter of seconds—presenting themselves as respectful journalism, falsified photos, or taken-out-of-context morsels of fact. The pervasiveness of social media has made fact-checking more of a reactive than a proactive role and generally permits distortions to become established before correction can occur.<br><br>The effects extend far beyond simple confusion. Manipulated media drive political action, fuel communal tensions, and erode trust in democratic institutions. If citizens cannot tell good sources of information from bad, democratic processes suffer, as public opinion is shaped by vetted facts rather than viral disinformation. In worst-case scenarios, disinformation has even prompted violence or destroyed health initiatives, as witnessed around the global pandemic.<br><br>Added to this problem is also the emergence of algorithm-fed aggregation of content, which further enriches echo chambers. The user is constantly given information that will most likely reinforce their current beliefs, creating a loop of feedback that legitimates falsity and bars dissonant truths. In the meantime, deepfakes and AI-generated content introduced an aspect of novelty in the crisis wherein fabrication is basically rendered indistinguishable from truth.<br><br>To combat this threat, however, calls for more than simply technical counter-response; it calls for media literacy, institutional disclosure, and a recasting of how truth is built and presented in a post-truth world. Without profound systemic change, the distinction between information and manipulation will always be blurry, threatening the very foundations of informed citizenship.<br><br><br>What does the author suggest is the greatest danger if fake media continues unchecked? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Decline of entertainment media"},"2":{"en":"Increase in fake literature"},"3":{"en":"Erosion of informed citizenship"},"4":{"en":"Loss of academic freedom"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The conclusion warns of threats to the foundations of informed citizenship.</b><br>Manipulation can obscure the distinction between reliable information and propaganda.<br>Entertainment, fake literature and academic freedom are not the central warning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Erosion of informed citizenship.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In an era of saturation with new media, the dissemination of counterfeit information in the media has become an irreversible threat to social cohesion. Though disinformation in the past was at least contained by geography and language, fabricated fiction in the present sweeps around the world in a matter of seconds—presenting themselves as respectful journalism, falsified photos, or taken-out-of-context morsels of fact. The pervasiveness of social media has made fact-checking more of a reactive than a proactive role and generally permits distortions to become established before correction can occur.<br><br>The effects extend far beyond simple confusion. Manipulated media drive political action, fuel communal tensions, and erode trust in democratic institutions. If citizens cannot tell good sources of information from bad, democratic processes suffer, as public opinion is shaped by vetted facts rather than viral disinformation. In worst-case scenarios, disinformation has even prompted violence or destroyed health initiatives, as witnessed around the global pandemic.<br><br>Added to this problem is also the emergence of algorithm-fed aggregation of content, which further enriches echo chambers. The user is constantly given information that will most likely reinforce their current beliefs, creating a loop of feedback that legitimates falsity and bars dissonant truths. In the meantime, deepfakes and AI-generated content introduced an aspect of novelty in the crisis wherein fabrication is basically rendered indistinguishable from truth.<br><br>To combat this threat, however, calls for more than simply technical counter-response; it calls for media literacy, institutional disclosure, and a recasting of how truth is built and presented in a post-truth world. Without profound systemic change, the distinction between information and manipulation will always be blurry, threatening the very foundations of informed citizenship.<br><br><br>The author uses the term “post-truth world” to highlight: [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A decline in reading habits"},"2":{"en":"A preference for emotion over fact"},"3":{"en":"A total collapse of media"},"4":{"en":"An age without news"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Post-truth = circumstances in which emotional appeal matters more than objective fact.</b><br>The passage describes manipulated media, political emotion and viral disinformation.<br>It does not discuss reading decline, total media collapse or absence of news.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A preference for emotion over fact.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In an era of saturation with new media, the dissemination of counterfeit information in the media has become an irreversible threat to social cohesion. Though disinformation in the past was at least contained by geography and language, fabricated fiction in the present sweeps around the world in a matter of seconds—presenting themselves as respectful journalism, falsified photos, or taken-out-of-context morsels of fact. The pervasiveness of social media has made fact-checking more of a reactive than a proactive role and generally permits distortions to become established before correction can occur.<br><br>The effects extend far beyond simple confusion. Manipulated media drive political action, fuel communal tensions, and erode trust in democratic institutions. If citizens cannot tell good sources of information from bad, democratic processes suffer, as public opinion is shaped by vetted facts rather than viral disinformation. In worst-case scenarios, disinformation has even prompted violence or destroyed health initiatives, as witnessed around the global pandemic.<br><br>Added to this problem is also the emergence of algorithm-fed aggregation of content, which further enriches echo chambers. The user is constantly given information that will most likely reinforce their current beliefs, creating a loop of feedback that legitimates falsity and bars dissonant truths. In the meantime, deepfakes and AI-generated content introduced an aspect of novelty in the crisis wherein fabrication is basically rendered indistinguishable from truth.<br><br>To combat this threat, however, calls for more than simply technical counter-response; it calls for media literacy, institutional disclosure, and a recasting of how truth is built and presented in a post-truth world. Without profound systemic change, the distinction between information and manipulation will always be blurry, threatening the very foundations of informed citizenship.<br><br><br>What is meant by “recasting how truth is built and presented”? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Creating new media outlets"},"2":{"en":"Promoting independent journalism only"},"3":{"en":"Rethinking media systems and knowledge legitimacy"},"4":{"en":"Encouraging AI journalism"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Recasting = fundamentally rethinking or restructuring.</b><br>The author calls for media literacy, disclosure and systemic change in how knowledge is validated.<br>Creating outlets, independent journalism alone or AI journalism are not the stated meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Rethinking media systems and knowledge legitimacy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In an era of saturation with new media, the dissemination of counterfeit information in the media has become an irreversible threat to social cohesion. Though disinformation in the past was at least contained by geography and language, fabricated fiction in the present sweeps around the world in a matter of seconds—presenting themselves as respectful journalism, falsified photos, or taken-out-of-context morsels of fact. The pervasiveness of social media has made fact-checking more of a reactive than a proactive role and generally permits distortions to become established before correction can occur.<br><br>The effects extend far beyond simple confusion. Manipulated media drive political action, fuel communal tensions, and erode trust in democratic institutions. If citizens cannot tell good sources of information from bad, democratic processes suffer, as public opinion is shaped by vetted facts rather than viral disinformation. In worst-case scenarios, disinformation has even prompted violence or destroyed health initiatives, as witnessed around the global pandemic.<br><br>Added to this problem is also the emergence of algorithm-fed aggregation of content, which further enriches echo chambers. The user is constantly given information that will most likely reinforce their current beliefs, creating a loop of feedback that legitimates falsity and bars dissonant truths. In the meantime, deepfakes and AI-generated content introduced an aspect of novelty in the crisis wherein fabrication is basically rendered indistinguishable from truth.<br><br>To combat this threat, however, calls for more than simply technical counter-response; it calls for media literacy, institutional disclosure, and a recasting of how truth is built and presented in a post-truth world. Without profound systemic change, the distinction between information and manipulation will always be blurry, threatening the very foundations of informed citizenship.<br><br><br>How do algorithm-driven platforms exacerbate the fake media problem? [SSC CGL 16/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They flag offensive content"},"2":{"en":"They ignore political content"},"3":{"en":"They reinforce user biases via echo chambers"},"4":{"en":"They encourage random viewpoints"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Algorithms feed users information that reinforces current beliefs.</b><br>This feedback loop creates echo chambers, legitimizes falsity and excludes dissonant truths.<br>Flagging content, ignoring politics and encouraging random views contradict the passage.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They reinforce user biases via echo chambers.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};